hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"11401","11370 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Muhammad ibn Rashid, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, from Ata and Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine the two prayers while traveling: Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha, without pursuing an enemy and without an enemy pursuing him."
"11402","11371 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated, Yahya ibn Kathir Abu al-Nadr narrated, Abd al-Karim narrated, Ata narrated, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear thunder, remember Allah, for it does not strike one who remembers."
"11403","11372 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Rashdin ibn Sad narrated, from Abi Sakhr, from Abd al-Karim Abi Umayyah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Wine is the mother of obscenities, and the greatest of major sins; whoever drinks it commits indecency with his mother, his maternal aunt, and his paternal aunt."
"11404","11373 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated, al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah Abu Hammad al-Hanafi narrated, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from Makkah to Mina on the day of Tarwiyah when the sun declined, and prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha; then he spent the night there until the morning of the day of Arafah. Then he went in the morning to Arafah and prayed Zuhr and Asr when the sun declined. Then he poured forth to Muzdalifah and prayed therein Maghrib and Isha together, with no voluntary prayer between them."
"11405","11374 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Muhammad ibn Maslamah narrated, from Ibn Arqam, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you bleeds from the nose during his prayer, let him leave, wash the blood from himself, then repeat his ablution and resume his prayer."
"11406","11375 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Hassani al-Wasiti narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani narrated, al-Mughirah ibn al-Ashath, an amir who was over us at Wasit, narrated, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the farewell Tawaf at night."
"11407","11376 - Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, my uncle Said ibn Isa ibn Talid narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ashras narrated; and Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: I read to Abdullah ibn Nafi, both from Abdullah ibn Umar, from his brother Ubaydullah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding al-Marwah: This is the place of sacrifice, and all the mountain passes of Makkah and its roads are places of sacrifice in Umrah."
"11408","11377 - Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated, Ayyub ibn Thabit narrated to me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The angels did not fight alongside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except on the day of Badr; apart from that they were reinforcements. And there were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of horses only two: one belonging to al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, and the other to Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi."
"11409","11378 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated, from Abi Farwah al-Rahawi, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not drink like the drinking of the camel; drink in two and three draughts, mention Allah when you drink, and praise Allah when you lift the vessel."
"11410","11379 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Khalid narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the shepherds to stone at night."
"11411","11380 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked."
"11412","11381 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only hastened between al-Safa and al-Marwah to show the polytheists his strength."
"11413","11382 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Muhassab is nothing; it is only a stop where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped."
"11414","11383 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep belonging to a freedwoman of Maymunah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is upon its people if they took its hide, tanned it, and benefited from it? They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is carrion. He said: Only its eating is forbidden."
"11415","11384 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A sheep died at the house of one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not tan its hide and make it into a waterskin."
"11416","11385 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Said ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated, he said: We read to Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead the weak of his family from Jam at night."
"11417","11386 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Umar ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated, my father narrated, from Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting and in Ihram."
"11418","11387 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi and Abu Khaythamah narrated, both said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus and Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in Ihram."
"11419","11388 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Warqa narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: And upon those who can bear it; he said: They are burdened with it; a ransom of feeding one needy person; and whoever volunteers good, increasing the food of another needy person, it is not abrogated; and it is better for him; no concession is granted in this except for the elderly who cannot fast, or a sick person who knows he will not recover."
"11420","11389 - Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-Ightiyal, then said: If it harmed anyone it would have harmed Persia and Rome. Ibn Bukayr said: And al-Ightiyal is that a man has intercourse with his wife while she is nursing."
"11421","11390 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha prayer one night, then came out with his head dripping water, and said: Were it not that I would burden my Ummah, I would have loved that this prayer be prayed at this time."
"11422","11391 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar and Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the prayer one night until part of the night had passed; then Umar came out and called him: The prayer, O Messenger of Allah; the women and children have slept. So he came out with water dripping from his side, wiping the water from his side and saying: Indeed it is the time, were it not that I would burden my Ummah."
"11423","11392 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells food, let him not sell it until he takes full possession of it. Thus Qabisah narrated it, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Amr, from Ata; and the companions of Hammad narrated it, from Hammad, from Amr, from Tawus; and likewise the companions of Amr ibn Dinar narrated it, and that is the correct version."
"11424","11393 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that a man bit the hand of a man in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so his front tooth was knocked out; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared it void. Thus Said ibn Amr narrated it, from Sufyan, from Amr, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, erring in it; and the companions of Ibn Uyaynah narrated it, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr, from Ata, from Safwan ibn Yala ibn Umayyah, from his father; and likewise the companions of Ata narrated it, and that is the correct version."
"11425","11394 - al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Mahdi al-Ubulli narrated, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated, Warqa narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution once."
"11426","11395 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Adhani al-Missisi narrated to us, al-Musayyab ibn Wadih narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded licking the bowl."
"11427","11396 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ayyub ibn Rashid narrated, Abd al-Ala narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah obligated them that one should fight ten, so that was hard upon them; then He lightened that from them, returning it to fighting the enemy when they are twice their number."
"11428","11397 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ayyub ibn Rashid narrated to me, Abd al-Ala narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: It is not for a prophet that he should have captives; then he recited until he reached: A great punishment; meaning the spoils of Badr before He made them lawful for them; saying: Were it not that I do not punish one who disobeys Me until I warn him in advance, there would have touched you for what you took a great punishment."
"11429","11398 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ayyub ibn Rashid narrated to me, Abd al-Ala narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: Say to those in your hands of the captives, until he reached: Taken from you. He said: al-Abbas used to say: By Allah, it was revealed concerning me, when I informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of my Islam, and asked him to reckon for me the twenty ounces found with me, but he refused to reckon them for me; so Allah gave me for the twenty ounces twenty slaves, each of them trading with my wealth in his hand, along with what I hope of the forgiveness of Allah."
"11430","11399 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, my father narrated, my father narrated, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated, Ata said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sheep among his Companions that day, and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas received a billy goat, which he slaughtered for himself. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at Arafah, he commanded Rabiah ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf, who stood beneath the forelegs of his she-camel, and he was a loud-voiced man, saying: Shout: Do you know what month this is? So he shouted, and the people said: The sacred month. He said: Shout: Do you know what land this is? They said: The sacred land. He said: Shout: Do you know what day this is? They said: The greater Hajj. He said: Shout. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden for you your blood and your wealth, like the sanctity of this month of yours, and like the sanctity of this land of yours, and like the sanctity of this day of yours. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) completed his Hajj; when he stood at Arafah he said: This is the standing place, and all of Arafah is a standing place. And when he stood upon Quzah he said: This is the standing place, and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place."
"11431","11400 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Warqa narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: This verse abrogated: Her waiting period is among her family, she may observe the waiting period wherever she wishes; the saying of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: Without expulsion. Ata said: If she wishes she may observe the waiting period among his family, and if she wishes she may go out, due to the saying of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: Then if they go out, there is no blame upon you for what they do with themselves."
"11432","11401 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, the companion of al-Maghazi, narrated, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Aban ibn Salih and Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Mujahid Abi al-Hajjaj, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah daughter of al-Harith during that journey of his while he was in the state of consecration; the one who married her to him was al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed at Makkah three days, then Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza came to him on the third day with a group of Quraysh, and Quraysh had entrusted him with expelling the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Makkah. They said: Your term has expired, so leave us. He said to them: What harm is it to you if you left me, so I consummate the marriage among you and prepare food for you which you attend? They said: We have no need of your food, so leave us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left."
"11433","11402 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray inside the House, but when he entered he fell prostrating, then raised his head, then supplicated."
"11434","11403 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Tai narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated, Abu Yusuf al-Qadi narrated, Nafi ibn Umar narrated to me, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrating from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the martyrs of Uhud, saying Takbir over them nine times nine, then seven times seven, then four times four, until he joined Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"11435","11404 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abu Musab narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated, from Abdullah ibn Amir al-Aslami, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the virgin seven days, and for the previously married three days."
"11436","11405 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj, and Ahmad ibn Rashdin, the Egyptians, narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Yahya ibn Salih al-Ubulli narrated, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Among what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated with during the Farewell Hajj was: O Allah, You hear my speech, see my place, and know my secret and my open; nothing of my affair is hidden from You. I am the wretched, needy, seeking aid, seeking refuge, fearful, apprehensive, acknowledging, confessing my sin. I ask You the asking of the humbled, beseech You the beseeching of the sinful lowly, and call upon You the calling of the fearful blind; one whose neck is humbled to You, whose eyes overflow for You, whose body is humbled, whose nose is in the dust for You. O Allah, do not make me wretched by my supplication to You, and be ever merciful to me, O best of those asked and best of givers."
"11437","11406 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rashdin ibn Sad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Tawus and Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the Tashahhud: The greetings, the good things, the prayers belong to Allah; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"11438","11407 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: It is the Sunnah for one who arrives at Makkah to circumambulate the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah before going out to Arafah; and it is the Sunnah for one of the people of Makkah to circumambulate the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah after returning from Mina."
"11439","11408 - Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of Arafat is a standing place, but keep away from the belly of Uranah; and all of Jam is a place of rites, but keep away from the belly of Muhassir."
"11440","11409 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me, Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is old and cannot perform Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: If he had a debt, would you settle it? He said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah is more deserving; perform Hajj on his behalf."
"11441","11410 - And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
"11442","11411 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh narrated, Shubah narrated, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A sheep belonging to Maymunah died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not benefit from it? They said: It is carrion. He said: Tanning the hide is its purification."
"11443","11412 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated, my father narrated to me, from Humayd ibn Qays, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, I have asked Allah for three things for you: I asked Him to make your upright firm, teach your ignorant, and guide your astray; and I asked Him to make you generous, valiant, merciful. If a man stood between the Corner and the Maqam, prayed and fasted, then died while hating the household of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may Allah be pleased with them, he would enter the Fire."
"11444","11413 - Mahmud ibn Ali al-Bazzar al-Asbahani narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi narrated, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated, from Asim ibn Umar, from Humayd ibn Qays, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded killing snakes in Ihram and the Haram."
"11445","11414 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, Abdullah ibn al-Muammal narrated, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters the House emerges forgiven."
"11446","11415 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, it will be called out: Where are the children of sixty? And it is the lifespan of which Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: Did We not grant you life long enough for whoever would be reminded to be reminded."
"11447","11416 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Sulaym narrated, Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: While I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to me: O boy, guard Allah and He will guard you; guard Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah; and when you seek help, seek help from Allah. The pens have been lifted and the pages have dried."
"11448","11417 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad Abu Jafar al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, from Ibn Khuthaym, Ata informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I circumambulated the House before stoning. He said: No harm."
"11449","11418 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ruasi narrated, from Abdullah ibn al-Muammal, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When people differ, justice lies with Mudar."
"11450","11419 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Hammal narrated, Hakkam ibn Salm narrated, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have no evil example; one who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit."
"11451","11420 - Ali ibn Bishr al-Maqarid al-Sanani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Urwah narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Sabbah narrated, from Mamar, from Umar ibn Habib, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When you see the crescent of the month of Ramadan, fast; then when you see it, break the fast."
"11452","11421 - Ubayd ibn Muhammad al-Kashwari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah ibn Damrah narrated, he said: We read to Mutarrif ibn Mazin, from Umar ibn Habib, he said: I heard Ata saying: Abdullah ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not see his Lord with his eyes; he only saw Him with his heart."
"11453","11422 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Nafi Darakht narrated, Muhammad ibn Mujib narrated, from Wuhayb ibn al-Ward al-Makki, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Exalted, has aided me with four ministers, chiefs. We said: O Messenger of Allah, who are these four? He said: Two from the people of heaven, and two from the people of earth. I said: Who are the two from the people of heaven? He said: Jibril and Mikail. We said: Who are the two from the people of earth? He said: Abu Bakr and Umar."
"11454","11423 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, Ata narrated to me, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third in addition to them; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"11455","11424 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha prayer one night until the people slept and woke up, and slept and woke up; then Umar ibn al-Khattab stood and said: The prayer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out with his head dripping water, and said: Were it not that this would burden my Ummah, I would have commanded them to pray it thus."
"11456","11425 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: A man vowed that he would circumambulate on his knees seven times. He said: Then Ibn Abbas said: They were not commanded to circumambulate crawling, but let him circumambulate for his knee seven times and for his foot seven times. I said: And he did not order him to offer any expiation? He said: No."
"11457","11426 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Ata informed me, saying: We attended with Ibn Abbas the funeral of Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: When you lift her bier, do not shake it and do not jolt it, and be gentle, for there were nine with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would apportion turns among eight and would not apportion a turn to one. Ata said: The one to whom he did not apportion a turn was Safiyyah bint Huyayy."
"11458","11427 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Ata informed me, he heard Ibn Abbas saying: If you are able that no one goes out early on the day of Fitr until he eats, let him do so. He said: So I have never abandoned eating before going out early since I heard that from Ibn Abbas; I eat from the edge of the tarifah. I said: What is the tarifah? He said: Thin flatbread; or I drink milk, or nabidh, or water. I said: On what basis do you interpret this? He said: I heard - I think from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: They would not go out until the forenoon had well extended, and they would say: We eat so that we are not hurried away from the prayer. He said: And sometimes I would go out early having tasted nothing but water - Ibn Abbas being the speaker."
"11459","11428 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, narrated to us Yahya ibn Salih al-Ayli, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow up between Hajj and Umrah, for they remove poverty and sins just as the bellows remove the dross of iron."
"11460","11429 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, narrated to us Yahya ibn Salih al-Ayli, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise."
"11461","11430 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us my father Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Rushdin ibn Sad, from Abu Hafs al-Makki, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked one day at Umar ibn al-Khattab and smiled at him, and said: O son of al-Khattab, do you know why I smiled at you? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Allah boasted to His angels on the night of Arafah about the people of Arafah in general, and boasted about you in particular."
"11462","11431 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq, narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I owe Allah a sacrificial camel and I am well-off but cannot find one. He said: Slaughter a sheep."
"11463","11432 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Wakii, narrated to us Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi, narrated to us al-Harith ibn Ghassan, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will raise the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner on the Day of Resurrection, and they will have two eyes, a tongue, and two lips, bearing witness for whoever touched them, with faithfulness."
"11464","11433 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) applied perfume before entering ihram."
"11465","11434 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us Dawud ibn Shabib, narrated to us Yahya ibn Abbad al-Sadi, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"11466","11435 - Narrated to us Ubayd al-Ijli, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban, narrated to us Abd al-Majid, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ibn Umm Maktum in charge of the prayer and other affairs of Madinah."
"11467","11436 - Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, told us Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi, narrated to us Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cover the faces of your dead, and do not resemble the Jews."
"11468","11437 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr, from Muawiyah ibn Amr, from al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ibn Jurayj and Ismail ibn Muslim, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked in the year he performed Hajj about the ramal, and he said: Allah has prescribed the sai upon you, so perform the sai."
"11469","11438 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar, narrated to us Hisham ibn Khalid, narrated to us Baqiyyah, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is afflicted with a calamity in his wealth or his body and conceals it and does not complain of it to people, it is incumbent upon Allah to forgive him."
"11470","11439 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ali, narrated to us Hisham ibn Khalid, narrated to us Baqiyyah, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah created the Garden of Eden, He created therein what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and what has never occurred to a human heart; then He said to it: Speak. And it said: Successful indeed are the believers."
"11471","11440 - Narrated to us Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari, narrated to us Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Hajjabi, narrated to us Nail ibn Najih, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ziyad, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing weapons in the lands of Islam or on the two Eids unless in the presence of an enemy."
"11472","11441 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us al-Ala ibn Amr al-Hanafi, narrated to us Yahya ibn Yazid al-Ashari, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love the Arabs for three things: because I am an Arab, and the Quran is Arabic, and the speech of the people of Paradise is Arabic."
"11473","11442 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Arzami, narrated to us Said ibn Khuthaym, from al-Awqas, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite aloud: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful."
"11474","11443 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Rushdin, narrated to us Abd al-Malik ibn Shuayb ibn al-Layth, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, al-Layth narrated to me, saying: Yahya ibn Said said: And Ibn Jurayj claimed that Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to him that a man came to Ibn Abbas and said: I vowed to slaughter myself. And Ibn Abbas said: You have had in the Messenger of Allah a good example, then he recited: And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice."
"11475","11444 - Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani, narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us Qudamah ibn Muhammad al-Ashjai, from Ismail ibn Shaybah al-Taifi, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon that made even the maidens in their chambers hear, and he said: O company of those who submitted with their tongues while faith has not entered their hearts, do not harm the believers and do not pursue their faults, for whoever pursues the fault of his brother, Allah will pursue his fault, and whomever Allah pursues for his fault will be disgraced even in the depth of his house."
"11476","11445 - Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us Qudamah ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Ismail ibn Shaybah, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five are of the practices of the Messengers: modesty, forbearance, cupping, perfuming, and marriage."
"11477","11446 - Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us Qudamah ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Ismail ibn Shaybah, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cupping is for toothache and drowsiness."
"11478","11447 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Rushdin ibn Sad al-Misri, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Aban al-Hashimi, narrated to us Umayr ibn Imran, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not righteousness."
"11479","11448 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Ukbari al-Wakii, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami, narrated to us Wuhayb, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The menstruating woman was permitted to depart when she menstruates."
"11480","11449 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Shuayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai, told us al-Husayn ibn Hurayth, narrated to us Nasr ibn Khalid, from al-Hasan ibn Rashid, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides breakfast to a fasting person has the like of his reward."
"11481","11450 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Tahhan al-Misri, narrated to us Abu Yusuf al-Jizi, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, who said: I was with Ibn Abbas when a man came to him and said: O Abu Abbas, what do you say about me? He said: And what could I say about you? He said: I work with a pen. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The owner of the pen will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in a coffin of fire, locked upon him with locks of fire, and he will look at his pen, wherein he expended it; if he expended it in obedience to Allah and His pleasure, the coffin will be opened from him for seventy autumns. The one who trims the pen and the one who prepares the inkwell."
"11482","11451 - Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri, narrated to us Yusuf ibn Adi, narrated to us Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The woman whose husband has died was forbidden perfume and adornment."
"11483","11452 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami, narrated to us Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of the gaps - meaning in prayer."
"11484","11453 - And narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Beware of the gaps - meaning in prayer - and he did not raise it to the Prophet."
"11485","11454 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih and Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah al-Utbi, both said: narrated to us Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, who said: narrated to us Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sanani, Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said one day: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my ummah. Ibn Abbas said: The foremost in good deeds enters Paradise without reckoning, the moderate enters Paradise by the mercy of Allah, and the wrongdoer to himself and the companions of the Heights enter Paradise by the intercession of Muhammad."
"11486","11455 - Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, my father narrated to me, saying: I read to Abu Qurrah al-Zubaydi, that Ibn Jurayj, Ata informed me, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw his Lord Almighty twice."
"11487","11456 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Muhammad al-Askari, narrated to us Sahl ibn Muhammad al-Askari, narrated to us Sahl ibn Uthman, narrated to us Abu Sad al-Saghani Muhammad ibn Muyassar, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained to him that she had been married off while unwilling, so she was removed from her husband; and she was previously married, and after that she married Abu Lubabah."
"11488","11457 - Narrated to us Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abd Allah al-Shami, narrated to us Salamah ibn Sinan, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When my ummah take lightly the sandals with straps - men and women - and patch their sandals, Allah will disown them."
"11489","11458 - Narrated to me Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi, narrated to us Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, Abu Muhammad narrated to me, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sacrificing at night."
"11490","11459 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ajlan Abu Shaykh al-Asbahani, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, narrated to us Adam ibn Abi Iyas, narrated to us Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever populates the left side of the mosque due to the scarcity of its people has two rewards."
"11491","11460 - Narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, narrated to us Abu Alqamah Abd Allah ibn Harun al-Farwi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Mansur, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of kindness in this world are the people of kindness in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter."
"11492","11461 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Said al-Razi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Mihran, narrated to us Artah Abu Hatim, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one has a greater favor upon me than Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him); he supported me with himself and his wealth, and married his daughter to me."
"11493","11462 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Raja, Yahya ibn Abi Sulayman al-Madani told us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not drink wine; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not sit at a table upon which wine is drunk; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not be alone with a woman with whom there is no mahram relationship."
"11494","11463 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Raja, Yahya ibn Sulayman told us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The black people were mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Leave me from the black people, for the black man is but his belly and his private part."
"11495","11464 - Narrated to us Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muhajir al-Misri, al-Harith ibn Miskin told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, Ibrahim ibn Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, from Kathir, freedman of Banu Makhzum, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) apportioned for eighty horses on the day of Hunayn two shares each."
"11496","11465 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman, narrated to us Hakim ibn Nafi, from Khusayf, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever drinks a sip of wine, Allah will not accept from him for three days, neither obligatory nor voluntary acts; and whoever drinks a cup, Allah will not accept from him for forty mornings; and the habitual wine-drinker - it is incumbent upon Allah to give him to drink from the river of al-Khabal. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the river of al-Khabal? He said: The pus of the people of Hellfire."
"11497","11466 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Ismail al-Razi, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Farra, narrated to us Abu Tawbah al-Harrani, narrated to us Khusayf, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to dye, he would take something of oil and saffron and rub it with his hands, then rub it upon his beard."
"11498","11467 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani, narrated to us Ayyub ibn Sulayman al-Hawzi, who said: I asked Ata ibn Abi Rabah about a man who mentioned a woman and said: The day I marry her she is divorced irrevocably. And Ata said: There is no divorce for one who does not own the marriage tie, and no emancipation for one who does not own the slave; he mentioned that from Ibn Abbas, and he attributed it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11499","11468 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dimashqi, my father narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Wahb, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."
"11500","11469 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us Hamzah ibn Ubayd Allah al-Thaqafi, narrated to us Abd al-Quddus ibn Habib, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding His saying: Marked ones: Marked; and the distinguishing mark of the angels on the day of Badr was black turbans, and on the day of Uhud red turbans."
"11501","11470 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Bakr al-Balisi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Musab al-Qarqasani, narrated to us al-Awzai, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no spot in which Allah is remembered with prayer but it boasts over the surrounding spots, and rejoices at the remembrance of Allah, its extent reaching to seven earths."
"11502","11471 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani, narrated to us Sallam al-Tawil, from al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sharp temper afflicts the best of my ummah."
"11503","11472 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Awzai - I heard it from him or was informed of it - from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man afflicted with smallpox became junub, so he washed and became chilled and died; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed, and he said: They killed him, may Allah kill them. Was not the cure for ignorance asking? Why did they not perform tayammum for him."
"11504","11473 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari, narrated to us Said ibn Hafs al-Nufayli, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Mihsan al-Ukkashi, narrated to us al-Awzai, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And to Him has submitted whoever is in the heavens and the earth, willingly and unwillingly - as for those in the heavens, they are the angels; and as for those on earth, they are those born upon Islam; and as for unwillingly, they are those brought from among the captives of the nations in chains and fetters, driven to Paradise while unwilling."
"11505","11474 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak, narrated to us Ismail ibn Ayyash, from al-Awzai, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) crossed the valleys and came with the sacrificial animals, and he was not to circumambulate the Kabah and between Safa and Marwah; and as for you, O people of Makkah, delay your circumambulation until you return."
"11506","11475 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban, narrated to us Yusuf ibn al-Fayd, from al-Awzai, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty sends down in every day and night one hundred and twenty mercies; sixty descend upon this House for those circumambulating, forty for those praying, and twenty for those looking."
"11507","11476 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Irs al-Misri, narrated to us Wahb Allah ibn Rizq Abu Hurayrah, narrated to us Bishr ibn Bakr, narrated to us al-Awzai, Ata narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah has an angel who, if it were said to him: Swallow the seven heavens and the earths in one mouthful, would do so; his glorification is: Glory be to You wherever You are."
"11508","11477 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Said al-Razi, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Hani al-Maqdisi, narrated to us Hani ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his uncle Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas and Abd Allah ibn Umar, both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the istikhara as he would teach us a surah of the Quran: O Allah, I seek good from You by Your knowledge, and I seek power from You by Your power, for You are able and I am not able, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen; O Allah, whatever decree You decree for me, make its outcome toward good."
"11509","11478 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Hisham ibn Ammar, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi al-Zuayziah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image of a statue, and the image-makers will be punished on the Day of Resurrection in the Fire; the Most Merciful will say to them: Stand up to what you fashioned; and they will continue to be punished until the image speaks, and it will not speak."
"11510","11479 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar, narrated to us Ishaq ibn al-Arkun, narrated to us Khulayd ibn Dalaj, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A security for the people of the earth against drowning is the rainbow, and a security for the people of the earth against dissension is allegiance to Quraysh, the people of Allah; so if a tribe of the Arabs opposes them, they become the party of Iblis."
"11511","11480 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar, narrated to us Ishaq ibn al-Arkun, narrated to us Abyan ibn Sufyan, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Wahshi, the killer of Hamzah, inviting him to Islam, so he sent back to him: O Muhammad, how do you invite me to your religion while you claim that whoever kills or associates partners with Allah or commits adultery meets retribution, his punishment doubled on the Day of Resurrection, abiding therein humiliated, and I have done that? So do you find any concession for me? Then Allah Almighty revealed: Except whoever repents and believes and does righteous work - for those, Allah will change their evils into good deeds, and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful. So Wahshi said: O Muhammad, this is a severe condition - except whoever repents and believes and does righteous work - and perhaps I cannot manage this. So Allah Almighty revealed: Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, and forgives what is besides that for whom He wills. So Wahshi said: O Muhammad, I see it is left to a will, and I do not know whether I will be forgiven or not; is there anything besides this? So Allah Almighty revealed: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah; Allah forgives all sins; He is the Forgiving, the Merciful. Wahshi said: This one; so he came and submitted. The people said: O Messenger of Allah, if we commit what Wahshi committed? He said: It is for the Muslims in general."
"11512","11481 - Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Sad ibn Yahya al-Raqqi, narrated to us Amir ibn Sayyar, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Ansari, Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a sick person wades in mercy; when he sits with him, mercy covers him; if he visits in the early part of the day, seventy thousand angels seek forgiveness for him until evening, and if he visits in the latter part of the day, seventy thousand angels seek forgiveness for him until morning. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, this is for the visitor, so what is for the sick? He said: Multiples of this."
"11513","11482 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Massisi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taraifi, narrated to us Abyan ibn Sufyan al-Maqdisi, from Khalifah ibn Sallam, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the Sudanese, for three of them are among the masters of the people of Paradise: Luqman the Wise, the Negus, and Bilal the caller to prayer. Abu al-Qasim said: He meant the Abyssinians."
"11514","11483 - Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Maymun al-Raqqi, narrated to us al-Hasan - meaning Abu al-Malih - from Habib ibn Abi Marzuq, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever arrives as a pilgrim and circumambulates the House and between Safa and Marwah, his Hajj has concluded and become an Umrah; and such is the practice of Allah and the practice of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11515","11484 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr, narrated to us Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, who said: I prayed Maghrib behind Ibn al-Zubayr, and he gave salams in two rakahs, then stood to receive the Stone, so they glorified Allah aloud at him and he returned, completed what remained, and prostrated two prostrations. So I asked Ibn Abbas, and he said: By Allah, his father, he did not deviate from the practice of his Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11516","11485 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah ibn Yahya, my grandfather Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, saying: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: We, the company of prophets, were commanded to hasten our breaking of the fast, delay our suhur, and place our right hands upon our left in prayer."
"11517","11486 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani, narrated to us Yaman ibn Said al-Massisi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Himyar, from Khalid ibn Humayd, from Khayr ibn Nuaym, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A gift to the ruler is misappropriation."
"11518","11487 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Zayd al-Khattabi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud, from his father, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it, they protect from me their blood and wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"11519","11488 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Jad al-Washsha, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakkar, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah, from Salim al-Aftas, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every inheritance that Islam overtakes, not yet divided, is upon the division of Islam."
"11520","11489 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Ali ibn Said, narrated to us Khalid ibn Hayyan, from Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his wives and the weak of his household, so they departed from Muzdalifah by night, then went until they stoned the Aqabah pillar."
"11521","11490 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani, narrated to us Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti, from Abd Allah ibn al-Muammil, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhaysin narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters the House enters into a good deed and leaves from an evil forgiven."
"11522","11491 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Bishr, narrated to us Hushaym, from Abd Allah ibn al-Muammil, from Ibn Muhaysin, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) requested from Suhayl ibn Amr water of Zamzam."
"11523","11492 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us Said ibn Sulayman, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn al-Muammil, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? And he said after three times: And those who shorten."
"11524","11493 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib, narrated to us Surayj ibn al-Numan al-Jawhari, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn al-Muammil, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived with the sacrificial animals, and circumambulated the House and between Safa and Marwah before standing at Arafah; as for you, O people of Makkah, delay your circumambulation until you return."
"11525","11494 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani, narrated to us Said ibn Sulayman, from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Abu Yaqub, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who marries without a guardian, her marriage is void; if he consummates with her, she has the dowry for what he made lawful of her private part; and if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"11526","11495 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki, both said: narrated to us al-Qanabi, narrated to us Umar ibn Qays, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill the geckos, even in the belly of the Kabah."
"11527","11496 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki, both said: narrated to us al-Qanabi, narrated to us Umar ibn Qays, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reaches Arafah before the rising of dawn has reached the Hajj."
"11528","11497 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Abu Asim, narrated to us Jafar ibn Yahya, from his uncle Umarah ibn Thawban, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best rows of men are the first, and the worst are the last; and the best rows of women are the last, and the worst are the first."
"11529","11498 - Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, narrated to us Rushdin ibn Sad, from Abu Sakhr, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Wine is the mother of obscenities and the greatest of major sins; whoever drinks it falls upon his mother, his maternal aunt, and his paternal aunt."
"11530","11499 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Ali ibn Said al-Raqqi, narrated to us Khalid ibn Habban, from Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his wives and the weak of his household, when they departed from Muzdalifah by night, then they went until they passed the Aqabah pillar."
"11531","11500 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki, narrated to us al-Hakam ibn Musa, narrated to us Yahya ibn Hamzah, al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Ata and Mujahid and Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram due to a pain he had, and used the tooth-stick while in ihram."
"11532","11501 - Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Salih, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: A sheep died, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the sheep's owner: Why did you not strip its skin, then tan it and benefit from it."
"11533","Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas. 11502 - Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who joins hair and the one for whom it is joined, the women imitating men, and the men imitating women."
"11534","11502 / 2 - Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you prevent his believing brother a piece of wood he places upon his wall."
"11535","11503 - Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died from the meat that the Jewish woman had poisoned; his aorta was cut off from the poison after a year, and he would say: I still feel from it a sensation."
"11536","11504 - Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Sad ibn Abi Waqqas a young she-goat of the goats and ordered him to sacrifice it."
"11537","11505 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri, narrated to us Abu Salih al-Harrani, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that some Muslims were with the polytheists, swelling the numbers of the polytheists, so an arrow comes in its shooting and strikes one of them and kills him, or he is struck and killed; so Allah Almighty revealed concerning them: Those whose souls the angels take while wronging themselves, they say: In what were you? They say: We were weak in the land - the verse."
"11538","11506 - Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Salih, al-Layth narrated to me, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ikrimah, Ibn Abbas informed me, that some Muslims were with polytheists, swelling the numbers of the polytheists against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so an arrow comes in its shooting and strikes one of them; and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Ibn Luhayah."
"11539","11507 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, my father narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were to stone anyone without clear proof, I would stone so-and-so; suspicion has appeared in her appearance, her speech, and who enters upon her."
"11540","11508 - Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Salih, al-Layth narrated to me (ha), and narrated to us Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, al-Layth narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder in the house of Maymunah bint al-Harith, then went out to prayer without performing ablution."
"11541","11509 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Rushdin, Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Iskandarani narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: May Allah reward Muhammad on our behalf as he deserves, tires seventy scribes for a thousand mornings."
"11542","11510 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Rushdin, Said ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed the two ihram garments at al-Tanim when he entered Makkah."
"11543","11511 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined between his wives in one cow for the sacrifice."
"11544","11512 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi, Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while in ihram."
"11545","11513 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Ismail ibn Yazid Abu Hazim al-Basri, narrated to us Hisham ibn Yusuf, Mamar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Muslim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the wife of Thabit ibn Qays sought khul, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to observe a waiting period of one menstruation."
"11546","11514 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Sharik, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The menstruating woman has gushes, and menstrual blood has an odor unlike others; when the period of menstruation ends, let one of you wash, then wash the blood from herself."
"11547","11515 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr told us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was placed in his pit, Shuqran, freedman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), took a woolen garment the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear and buried it with him in the grave, saying: No one shall wear it after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11548","11516 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Those who descended into the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Ali, al-Fadl and Qutham the two sons of al-Abbas, and Shuqran, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Aws ibn Khawli said to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): O Ali, I adjure you by Allah concerning our share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Descend with the people; so he descended, and they were five."
"11549","11517 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi ibn Yazid told us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver two sermons on Friday standing, sitting between them."
"11550","11518 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn al-Samida al-Antaki, Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the sermon on Friday and on Fitr and Adha upon the pulpit; when the caller to prayer fell silent on Friday, he stood and preached."
"11551","11519 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratis, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us (ha), and narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Ibn al-Asbahani and Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, both said: Sharik narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any slave woman who bears a child from her master is free after his death."
"11552","11520 - Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, both said: Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a garment wrapped around him, shielding himself with its excess from the heat of the ground."
"11553","11521 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri, Abd al-Malik ibn Shuayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Sharik ibn Abd Allah, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in a single garment, shielding himself with its excess from the heat and cold of the ground."
"11554","11522 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Husayn ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abbas informed me, from Ikrimah and Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: Shall I inform you of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? We said: Yes. He said: When the sun had declined for him in his dwelling, he would combine Zuhr and Asr before mounting; if it had not declined for him in his dwelling, he would travel until when it was Asr time he would descend and combine Zuhr and Asr; and when Maghrib came while he was in his dwelling, he would combine it with Isha; and if it had not come for him in his dwelling, he would mount until when Isha came he would descend and combine the two. Abd al-Razzaq said: And Ibn al-Miqdam said to me: We never heard this from Ibn Jurayj, nor did anyone but you bring it."
"11555","11523 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami al-Misri, Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Musa ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling and departed after the sun had declined, he would combine Zuhr and Asr; and if he departed before that, he would combine the two at the time of Asr."
"11556","11524 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"11557","11525 - Narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, Yusuf ibn Salman al-Mazini narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to mount after the sun had declined, would combine Zuhr and Asr before mounting; and when he wanted to mount before the Maghrib time, he would delay Maghrib until combining it with Isha."
"11558","11526 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"11559","11527 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Said al-Razi, Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Madini narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lut, kill the doer and the one done to."
"11560","11528 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to encourage the night prayer until he said: Even a single rakah; then he went out to prayer, and there was a man praying while the prayer was being established, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two prayers together?"
"11561","11529 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Mualla, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"11562","11530 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the night prayer and encouraged it until he said: Upon you is the night prayer, even a single rakah; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and there was a man bowing after the prayer had been established, and he also said: Will you not desist; two prayers together?"
"11563","11531 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Said al-Razi, Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: O Allah, grant Ibn Abbas wisdom and teach him interpretation."
"11564","11532 - Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, Musaddad narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Qays, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached and said: Allah Almighty has given every holder of a right his right; indeed Allah has ordained obligations, established practices, set limits, permitted the lawful and forbade the unlawful, and legislated the religion and made it easy, lenient, and spacious, and did not make it narrow; indeed there is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, no religion for one who has no covenant; whoever breaks my covenant shall not attain my intercession nor arrive at my Basin; indeed Allah Almighty has not permitted killing except in three: an apostate after faith, an adulterer after chastity, or a killer of a soul, so he is killed for his killing; have I conveyed?"
"11565","11533 - Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, Musaddad narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating, from Hanash, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When a wind blew violently, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would face it, kneel upon his knees, stretch out his hands, and say: O Allah, I ask You the good of this wind and the good of what it was sent with; O Allah, make it mercy and do not make it punishment; O Allah, make them winds and do not make it a wind. And narrated to us Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Ali al-Rahbi, who is al-Husayn ibn Qays, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When a wind blew violently, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would face it with his face, kneel upon his knees, stretch with his hands, and say the same."
"11566","11534 - Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, Musaddad narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Qays (ha), and narrated to us Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Ali al-Rahbi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever walks to the ruler of Allah on earth to humiliate him, Allah will humiliate his neck on the Day of Resurrection, besides what is stored for him in the Hereafter. Muslim added: And the ruler of Allah is the Book of Allah and the practice of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11567","11535 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Qays, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to those in charge of measures and scales: You have been entrusted with a matter in which the former nations perished."
"11568","11536 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur narrated to us, Husayn ibn Qays narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Iblis sends his strongest and most powerful companions to one who does good with his wealth."
"11569","11537 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Hanash, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Dharr: Which handholds of faith - I think he said - are firmest? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Allegiance for Allah, enmity for Allah, love for Allah, and hatred for Allah."
"11570","11538 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Hanash, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever drinks a beverage that removes from him the intellect he was given has come to a door of the major sins."
"11571","11539 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating, from Hanash, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever aids falsehood to refute with his falsehood a truth has become free of the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11572","11540 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, saying: And Hanash narrated, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever combines two prayers without excuse has come to a door of the major sins."
"11573","11541 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, saying: And Hanash narrated, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever bears testimony so that the wealth of a Muslim is made lawful thereby or blood is shed thereby has made the Fire incumbent."
"11574","11542 - Narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us (ha), and narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us (ha), and narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, all said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Hanash, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned, saying: No Muslim takes an orphan among Muslims to his food and drink but enters Paradise outright, unless he commits a sin that is not forgiven; and whoever has his two precious ones taken and is patient and reckons the reward, has no reward with Me but Paradise. It was said: And what are his two precious ones? He said: His two eyes. He said: And whoever raises three daughters, spends upon them, and disciplines them well, Allah admits him to Paradise. A Bedouin man said: Or two? He said: Or two. Ibn Abbas said: This is among the excellent and rare of hadith."
"11575","11543 - Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, Musaddad narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating, from Hanash, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Nawfal ibn al-Harith sent his two sons to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying to them: Go to your uncle; perhaps he will employ you in the charities, so you may gain something and marry. They met Ali, who said: Where are you heading? They told him of their need, so he said to them: Return. They returned; in the evening he ordered them to go to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they reached the door, they sought permission, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Aishah: Lower your curtain; admit to me my two cousins. They told the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of their need, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Nothing of the charities is lawful for you, O people of the House, nor the washings of hands; you have in the fifth of the fifth what enriches you - or: suffices you."
"11576","11544 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hanash ibn Qays, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No flesh grown from unlawful earnings enters Paradise."
"11577","11545 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was to the extent that those in the chamber could hear him."
"11578","11546 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratis and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf, both said: Said ibn Abi Maryam told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad and Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, both said: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse whoever takes others than his freedmen as allies; may Allah curse whoever changes the boundaries of the earth; may Allah curse whoever misleads a blind man from the path; may Allah curse whoever curses his parents; may Allah curse whoever slaughters for other than Allah; may Allah curse whoever commits bestiality; may Allah curse whoever does the deed of the people of Lut; may Allah curse whoever does the deed of the people of Lut; may Allah curse whoever does the deed of the people of Lut."
"11579","11547 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, al-Qanabi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man held fast to a debtor of his for ten dinars, saying: By Allah, I have no payment with which to pay you today. He said: By Allah, I will not leave you until you pay or bring a guarantor to guarantee for you. He said: By Allah, I have no payment, and I find no one to guarantee for me. He said: So he dragged him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, this man held fast to me, and I asked him to wait one month, but he refused until I pay him or bring him a guarantor. I said: By Allah, I find no guarantor, and I have no payment today. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you wait for him but one month? He said: No. He said: Then I guarantee it for you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) guaranteed it, and the man went and brought him the amount he had promised; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: From where did you get this gold? He said: From a mine. He said: Then go, we have no need of it, and there is no good in it; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid it on his behalf."
"11580","11548 - Narrated to us Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi al-Misri, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about the Friday ghusl, is it obligatory? He said: No, but it is more beloved to me to perform ghusl; whoever does not perform ghusl, it is not obligatory upon him; and I shall tell you how this was: People were hard-pressed, wearing wool and working on their backs, and their mosque was narrow, and the roof was but a trellis. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one hot day, having sweated in that wool until odors arose and until thereby some of them harmed others; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found those odors, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, when this day comes, perform ghusl, and let each of you touch the best oil and perfume he finds."
"11581","11549 - Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Twenty men of the freedmen witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11582","11550 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah, Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Drinkers were beaten in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with hands, sandals, and sticks."
"11583","11551 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dili, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) caught on a tree on the day of Hunayn, with people gathered upon him asking him of the spoils; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thought they had held his cloak, and said: Release my cloak; do you wish to make me out miserly? By Allah, if Allah bestows upon you like the trees of Tihamah in livestock, I would divide it among you; then you would not find me miserly, cowardly, or lying. They said: But a samurah tree had caught his clothes, so they freed him."
"11584","11552 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged allegiance to him in the mosque, then left; he stood, spread his legs, then urinated. People rushed at him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not interrupt the man's urination. Then he said: Are you not a Muslim? He said: Yes. He said: What carried you to urinate in our mosque? He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I thought it but a patch of open ground, so I urinated in it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a bucket of water, and it was poured over his urine."
"11585","11553 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cheats us is not of us, and whoever shoots at us by night is not of us."
"11586","11554 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, author of the military expeditions, narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked with them to Baqi al-Gharqad, then dispatched them, saying: Go in the name of Allah; O Allah, aid them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to his house - meaning concerning the killing of Ibn al-Ashraf."
"11587","11555 - Narrated to us Abu Shuayb al-Harrani, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked with them, and he mentioned the like of it."
"11588","11556 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man to whom it seems in his prayer that he has broken wind though he has not, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer until he opens his seat, so it seems to him that he has broken wind though he has not; if one of you finds that, let him not leave until he hears the sound of that with his ear or finds its odor with his nose."
"11589","11557 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ismail ibn Subayh narrated to us, from Abu Uways, from Thawr ibn Zayd and Musa ibn Maysarah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the woman with prolonged bleeding, and he said: That is a kick of Satan in her womb."
"11590","11558 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, Dirar ibn Surad Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deceives in horse racing on race day is not of us."
"11591","11559 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to glance in prayer right and left, without turning from it behind his back."
"11592","11560 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna Abu Yala al-Mawsili, Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abd Allah, freedman of Ghufrah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O boy, shall I not teach you something by which Allah will benefit you? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Guard Allah and He will guard you; guard Allah and you will find Him before you; know Allah in ease and He will know you in hardship; when you ask, ask Allah, and when you seek help, seek help from Allah; the Pen has dried upon what will be until the Day of Resurrection; if the creatures strove to benefit you with something Allah has not written for you, they could not do so, and if the creatures strove to harm you with something Allah has not written against you, they could not do so."
"11593","11561 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah al-Ashhali narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent sheep to Sad ibn Abi Waqqas to divide among his companions, and they were performing tamattu; a he-goat remained, so Sad ibn Abi Waqqas sacrificed it in his tamattu."
"11594","11562 - Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that when he dispatched his armies he would say: Go forth in the name of Allah; fight in the way of Allah those who disbelieve in Allah; do not transgress, do not mutilate, do not kill children, nor the companions of the monasteries."
"11595","11563 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us (ha). And narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, both said: Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach them from all pains and from fever this supplication: In the name of Allah the Great; I seek refuge with Allah the Magnificent from the evil of every spurting vein, and from the evil of the heat of the Fire."
"11596","11564 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Musa ibn Harun, both said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: No prophet ever had a wet dream; wet dreams are only from Satan."
"11597","11565 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever commits intercourse with a mahram relative, kill him."
"11598","11566 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a dog laps in a vessel, it is washed seven times."
"11599","11567 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub al-Ahwazi, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the muhallil, and he said: There is no marriage but a marriage of desire, not a marriage of deceit, nor one mocking the Book of Allah who has not tasted the little honey."
"11600","11568 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever commits bestiality, kill him and kill it; and whoever commits with a man, kill him - meaning the deed of the people of Lut."
"11601","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Qawwas narrated to us: Abd al-Majid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Ibrahim ibn Dawud ibn al-Husayn informed me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill the doer and the one to whom it is done, the deed of the people of Lut, and the one who approaches an animal, and the one who approaches a female mahram."
"11602","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abu Muslim al-Mustamli Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus narrated to us: Ma'n ibn Isa narrated to us: Kharijah ibn Abd Allah ibn Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of Arafah is a standing place, and keep away from al-Sifah."
"11603","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Umar al-Razi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best? He said: A tolerant Hanifiyyah."
"11604","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which religions are most beloved to Allah? He said: The tolerant Hanifiyyah."
"11605","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The verses in al-Ma'idah, {So judge between them with justice; indeed Allah loves those who act justly}, were revealed only concerning blood money among Banu Qurayzah and Banu al-Nadir. The tribe of Banu al-Nadir had nobility and paid the full blood money, while Banu Qurayzah paid half the blood money, and they sought judgment about that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Allah revealed that concerning them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held them to the truth in that and made the blood money equal."
"11606","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, both saying: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, the author of al-Maghazi, narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: This verse, {And do not recite loudly in your prayer nor whisper it, but seek a way between that}, was revealed only because of those people. That is, do not recite your prayer loudly lest they disperse away from you, and do not whisper it lest it not be heard by one who loves to hear it among those who eavesdrop upon it apart from them; perhaps they would call to some of what is heard and benefit from it."
"11607","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned Zaynab, his daughter, to her husband with her first marriage, and did not introduce anything new."
"11608","Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated to us: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no harm nor reciprocal harm."
"11609","Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed a horned, large-eyed, intact ram."
"11610","Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A believer does not steal from the spoils."
"11611","Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed on Friday while standing."
"11612","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man says to a man, O effeminate, flog him twenty, and if a man says to a man, O Jew, flog him twenty."
"11613","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail al-Sakuni narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of madamin and malaqih and habal al-habalah."
"11614","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A person in ihram was permitted to kill the snake, the scorpion, the mouse, the kite, and the vicious dog."
"11615","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the two Eids before the sermon."
"11616","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Ali came from Yemen and met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Juhfah. He said: With what did you enter ihram, O Ali? He said: With the same as you entered ihram with, O Messenger of Allah. So he made him a partner in his sacrificial animals."
"11617","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man to collect charity, called Ibn al-Utbiyyah. He collected and returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I neither transgressed nor left any due, and a gift was given to me and I accepted the gift. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat on the pulpit and said: I send men for charity, then one of them comes and says: By Allah, I neither transgressed nor left them any due, and a gift was given to me and I accepted the gift. Would he not sit in a small enclosure and wait what is gifted to him? Beware that one of you comes with a camel growling on his neck, or a cow mooing, or a sheep bleating. Then he raised his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was seen, then said: O Allah, have I conveyed?"
"11618","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took al-Fadl ibn Abbas behind him, and he kept reciting the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah."
"11619","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Quraysh asked permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the atirah. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we slaughter the atirah in Rajab? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: An atirah like that of Jahiliyyah? But whoever among you loves to slaughter for Allah and eat and give charity, let him do so. And their atirah was that they slaughtered and then took the blood of their sacrifices and wiped it on the heads of their idols."
"11620","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent on the days of Mina a crier proclaiming: Do not fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking and marital relations. And bial means intercourse with women."
"11621","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us: Sad ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us: Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from al-Fadl ibn Ata, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The south wind never moves a trace of valley rain but that it makes it flow."
"11622","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us: Muadh ibn Hani narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated to us: al-Abbas ibn Abd Allah ibn Mabad narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear his ring on his right hand."
"11623","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated to us: al-Walid ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Circumcision is a sunnah for men and an honor for women."
"11624","Ubayd ibn Ghannam ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us (h), and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, both saying: Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yaqub ibn Utbah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt truthful in two verses of his poetry. Upon his saying, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth. And upon his saying, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth."
"11625","Al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya al-Mutarriz and Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, both saying: Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Hasan ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting."
"11626","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Nasa'i al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Amr ibn al-As, may Allah be pleased with him, led the people in prayer while in a state of major impurity. When they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they mentioned that to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and asked him about that. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I feared the cold would kill me, and Allah Almighty said, {And do not kill yourselves; indeed Allah is Merciful to you}. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent toward him."
"11627","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Nasa'i narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: When a man said to a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), O Jew, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged him twenty lashes."
"11628","Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no celibacy in Islam."
"11629","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya ibn Hassan al-Kufi narrated to us: Hisham ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Umar ibn Ata, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Provision is sustenance and a mount."
"11630","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Rukanah informed me: Ikrimah informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fix a hadd for wine. Ibn Abbas said: And a man drank an intoxicant and was found staggering in a mountain pass, so he was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he came alongside the house of al-Abbas, he slipped away and al-Abbas entered and embraced him. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he laughed and said: Did he do it? And he did not ask about him."
"11631","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj: al-Hakam ibn Aban informed me, from Ikrimah, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, who said: Ibn Abbas said: When the illness of Abd Allah ibn Ubayy in which he died occurred, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him, and they exchanged words between them. Abd Allah said: I have understood what you say; bestow favor upon me and shroud me in your shirt and pray over me. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded him in that shirt of his and prayed over him. Ibn Abbas said: And Allah knows best what prayer it was, and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never deceived any person."
"11632","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Humayd ibn Hammad ibn Khuwar narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I declared zihar upon my wife and I approached her before expiating. He said: And what carried you to that? He said: I saw her leg in the moonlight and I had intercourse with her. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep away from her until you expiate."
"11633","Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had declared zihar upon his wife and then had intercourse with her. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I declared zihar upon my wife and I had intercourse with her before expiating. He said: And what carried you to that, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I saw her anklet in the moonlight. He said: Do not approach her until you do what Allah Almighty commanded you."
"11634","Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother died and she did not perform Hajj nor leave a bequest; shall I perform Hajj on her behalf? He said: What do you think, if your mother had a debt and you paid it?"
"11635","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Isa al-Hanafi narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: While Umm Salamah was one night lying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she got up as if concealing herself. He said: What is the matter with you, have you begun menstruating? She said: Yes. He said: No harm; take your ablution water and return to your place."
"11636","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Isa narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the best of you call the adhan for you, and let your reciters lead you in prayer."
"11637","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Isa narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, used to bathe from one vessel and would contend for the water."
"11638","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us (h), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both saying: Husayn ibn Isa narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion. Then a Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, we take a mangy sheep and cast it among the flock and they become mangy. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bedouin, who made the first one mangy?"
"11639","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban informed us: My father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, that he said: There is no recitation in Zuhr and Asr except with the Fatihat al-Kitab. Then Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to recite, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conveyed what Allah revealed of the messages of his Lord."
"11640","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhimari narrated to us: Fa'id ibn Umar narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman used to pick up litter from the mosque and she died, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not informed of her burial. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of your dead dies, inform me. And he prayed over her and said: I have seen her in Paradise, for what she used to pick up of litter from the mosque."
"11641","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Ayan narrated to me, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a father looks at his child and it delights him, the child gets the freeing of a slave. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he looks three hundred and sixty times? He said: Allah is Greater."
"11642","Al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Isa al-Hanafi narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The umm al-walad is free even if it is a miscarriage."
"11643","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Allah Almighty favored Muhammad over the people of the heaven and the people of the earth. A man said to him: O Abu Abbas, what is his superiority over the people of the heaven? He said: Allah Almighty says to the people of the heaven, {And whoever of them says, I am a god besides Him, We shall recompense him with Hell; thus We recompense the wrongdoers}. And Allah Almighty said to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), {Indeed We have granted you a clear victory, that Allah may forgive you your former and latter sins}, the verse. It was said to him: O Abu Abbas, what is his superiority over the prophets? He said: Allah Almighty says, {And We sent no messenger except in the tongue of his people}. And Allah Almighty said to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), {And We sent you not except to all mankind as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner}. So Allah sent him to the jinn and mankind."
"11644","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Adani narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, who said: Ibn Abbas said: I never heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and Asr, nor did he command us, though he conveyed."
"11645","Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I was beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day the sun eclipsed, and I did not hear any recitation from him."
"11646","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Hafs ibn Umar al-Adani narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he stood for a long time, then bowed for a long time, then stood for a long time, then bowed for a long time, then prostrated, then repeated the like of it."
"11647","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When this verse was revealed, {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned}, Persia sent to Quraysh to dispute with Muhammad and say to him: What you slaughter with your hand with a knife is lawful, and what Allah slaughters with a sword of gold is unlawful. Then this verse was revealed, {And indeed the devils inspire their allies to dispute with you}. He said: The devils are from Persia, and their allies are from Quraysh."
"11648","Abu Shaykh Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ajlan al-Asbahani narrated to us: Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah Almighty said: Whoever knows that I have power to forgive sins, I forgive him and I do not care, so long as he does not associate anything with Me."
"11649","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ajlan narrated to us: Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I would love that it be in the heart of every person of my ummah, meaning, {Blessed is He in Whose hand is dominion}."
"11650","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah, who said: Whoever's religion differs from the religion of the Muslims, strike his neck. And he said: When he testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, there is no way against him except that he commits something for which a hadd is established upon him."
"11651","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, who said: One of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died in Madinah - Ishaq said: I think he named her Safiyyah bint Huyayy - so I came to Ibn Abbas and informed him, and he prostrated. I said to him: Do you prostrate when the sun has not yet risen? Ibn Abbas said: May you have no mother, do you not know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the sign, prostrate. And what sign is greater than the Mothers of the Believers departing from among us while we are alive?"
"11652","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Hamid ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has seen his Lord. Ikrimah said: O Abu Abbas, does not Allah say, {Eyes do not perceive Him, while He perceives eyes}? Ibn Abbas said: May you have no mother, that is only when He is alone in a manner that no sight can withstand."
"11653","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashshar al-Nasa'i narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban informed us, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A short spear was planted before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed toward it, while camel litters passed behind it."
"11654","Isa ibn al-Qasim al-Saydalani al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam al-Marwazi narrated to us: Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Adani narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every tie and lineage will be cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my tie and my lineage."
"11655","Isa ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: Musa ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Adani narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Abbas: O my uncle, shall I not teach you? Shall I not grant you? Shall I not inform you? Shall I not do for you ten qualities: if you do that, Allah will forgive you your sin, its first and last, old and new, secret and open, minor and major, mistaken and deliberate - that you pray four rakahs, reciting in each rakah the Fatihat al-Kitab and a surah. When you finish the recitation in the first rakah, say while standing: Subhan Allah, al-hamdu lillah, la ilaha illa Allah, Allahu Akbar, fifteen times. Then bow and say while bowing ten times. Then raise your head and say while standing ten times. Then prostrate and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say while sitting ten times. Then prostrate and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say it ten times. That is seventy-five. Do that in four rakahs. Even if your sins were like the foam of the sea or the sand of Alij, Allah will forgive them for you."
"11656","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us: Hafs ibn Umar al-Adani narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer, nor does he steal when he steals while he is a believer, nor does he plunder plunder while he is a believer."
"11657","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Zama'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on a mat."
"11658","Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Adam narrated to us (h), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, both saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Zama'ah ibn Salih, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek help with the midday rest for standing at night, and with the pre-dawn meal for fasting the day."
"11659","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Zama'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not come to women at night - meaning when one of you returns from a journey, he should not come to his family except by day. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from a journey, and two men went ahead after the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and came to their families, and each one found a man with his wife."
"11660","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"11661","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us: al-Hudhayl ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The death of the stranger is martyrdom."
"11662","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us (h), and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi and Shihab ibn Abbad narrated to us, all saying: Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four umrahs: the Umrah of al-Hudaybiyyah, the Umrah of al-Qada the next year, his third Umrah from al-Jiranah, and his fourth Umrah which was with his Hajj."
"11663","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died and did not leave a bequest; will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes."
"11664","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us: Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that his mother had died: will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes. He said: I have a garden of date palms, and I call you to witness that I have given it in charity on her behalf. Rawh said: Al-makhrafah means date palms."
"11665","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Jawwaz narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - and Sufyan said another time: Ikrimah informed me, he said: When Abu Sufyan and the polytheists turned back from Uhud and reached al-Rawha, they said: You neither killed Muhammad nor made the maidens ride behind you; evil is what you have done. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he called the people forth and they responded until they reached Hamra al-Asad or the well of Abu Uyaynah. Then Allah Almighty revealed, {Those who responded to Allah and the Messenger after injury had befallen them}. Abu Sufyan had said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your appointment is the fair of Badr where you killed our companions. As for the coward, he turned back, and as for the brave, he took the preparation for fighting and trade. They came to it and found no one there, and they traded. Then Allah Almighty revealed, {So they returned with favor from Allah and bounty; no harm touched them}."
"11666","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: Rawh ibn Ubad informed us: Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Its thorny trees shall not be cut, its game shall not be frightened, its herbage shall not be cut, and its lost property is not lawful except for one who announces it. Al-Abbas said: Except idhkhir. He said: Except idhkhir."
"11667","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us: Tahir ibn Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has made Makkah sacred; it was not lawful for anyone before me, nor is it lawful for anyone after me. It was made lawful for me only for an hour of a day, then it is sacred by the sanctity of Allah: its trees shall not be cut, its game shall not be frightened, and its herbage shall not be cut. Al-Abbas said: Except idhkhir. He said: Except idhkhir."
"11668","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah's anger is severe upon one whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kills, and upon one who causes the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to bleed."
"11669","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Ali consummated marriage with Fatimah with a body armor of iron."
"11670","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu al-Jawza Ahmad ibn Uthman narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever listens to the talk of a people while they dislike it, molten lead shall be poured into his ear on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever makes his eyes see in a dream what they did not see will be tasked to tie a grain of barley."
"11671","Musa ibn Sahl Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Dinar: he informed him, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked a man: Where did you stay? He said: With so-and-so woman. He said: Did she close her door upon you? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that."
"11672","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: Abu Amir al-Aqadi informed us: Zama'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man arrived from a journey, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You stayed with so-and-so woman and entered upon her?! And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that."
"11673","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashshar al-Nasa'i narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi informed us: Ibrahim ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I marvel at the patience of my brother Yusuf and his nobility, and Allah forgive him, when he was sent for to interpret the dream. Had I been in his place I would not have done so until I came out. And I marvel at his patience and his nobility, and Allah forgive him: he was brought forth to come out but did not come out until he told them his excuse. Had I been in his place I would have rushed to the door. And were it not for the word, he would not have remained in prison, seeking relief from other than Allah: his saying, {Mention me to your lord}."
"11674","Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us: Said ibn Mansur narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying, {And We made the vision which We showed you only a trial for people}. He said: It is a vision the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw on the night he was taken by night; it is not a dream vision."
"11675","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The moon eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: The moon has been bewitched. Then was revealed, {The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split}, up to His saying, {continuing}."
"11676","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he mentioned something like the hadith of Ibn Jurayj."
"11677","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Ali entered upon Fatimah on the day of Uhud and said: Take this sword, not blameworthy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you fought well, Sahl ibn Hunayf and Abu Dujanah Simak ibn Kharashah indeed fought well."
"11678","Al-Muntasir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntasir al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Yunus ibn Sulayman al-Hammal narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Huyayy ibn Akhtab and Kab ibn al-Ashraf came to Makkah to Quraysh and allied with them to fight the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said to them: You are people of ancient knowledge and people of the Book; inform us about us and about Muhammad. They said: What are you and what is Muhammad? They said: We slaughter fat camels, give milk over water, free captives, give drink to pilgrims, and join ties of kinship. They said: What is Muhammad? They said: A cut-off one who severed our kinship, followed by the thieves of pilgrims, Banu Ghifar. They said: Rather you are better than him and more guided in way. Then Allah Almighty revealed, {Have you not seen those given a portion of the Book; they believe in al-jibt and al-taghut}, to the end of the verse."
"11679","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Khuwar narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, who said: A man asked Ibn Abbas: What suffices for ghusl? He said: A sa and a mudd for wudu. A man said: It does not suffice me. He said: May you have no mother, it suffices one better than you, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11680","Ahmad ibn al-Jarudi al-Asbahani and Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, both saying: Malik ibn Sad al-Qaysi narrated to us: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah has cursed men who imitate women, and cursed women who imitate men."
"11681","Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban al-Adami al-Shirazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Hakim al-Razi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Makki narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: We used to eat and drink and bathe, then go out to the prayer place."
"11682","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi narrated to us: Mani' ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Abdi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, who said: I saw Abd Allah ibn Abbas eating at Arafah for a time, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fast it, nor Abu Bakr nor Umar."
"11683","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah and Abu Mabad, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man was commanded to hold himself firm, ten against a hundred, when the Muslims were few. When the Muslims became many, Allah Almighty commanded a man to hold firm against two men, ten against twenty, and a hundred against two hundred."
"11684","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both saying: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The first of what was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was that it was said to him: Cover yourself. And his private part was not seen after that."
"11685","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Waki'i narrated to us: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out cheerful and said: Allah Almighty has added for you a prayer, and it is al-witr."
"11686","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Waki'i narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I forbade you from visiting graves, so visit them, and do not say obscene speech. I forbade you from the meat of sacrifices after three days, so eat and keep. I forbade you from nabidh, so drink, but do not drink intoxicant."
"11687","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated to us: Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in his sandals."
"11688","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of gharar."
"11689","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in a house with nothing on him but a waist wrapper, and he cast it between his legs with his thighs exposed. Abu Bakr came asking permission and he permitted him and he entered. Then Umar came and he permitted him and he entered. Then Uthman came and he permitted him, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, he stood up quickly until he entered the house. That was hard upon A'ishah. When the people left, she said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr and Umar entered and you did not change your state, but when Uthman entered you stood up. He said: O A'ishah, shall I not be shy of one whom the angels are shy of? The angels are shy of Uthman."
"11690","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us (h), and Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, both saying: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Nadr Abu Umar narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, strengthen Islam with Umar ibn al-Khattab or with Abu Jahl ibn Hisham. Abu Kurayb added in his hadith: Umar awoke in the morning and went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and embraced Islam that day. Abu Kurayb said in his hadith: O Allah, honor Islam."
"11691","Abd al-Salam ibn Sahl al-Sukkari narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: al-Nadr Abu Umar narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man prayed behind the rows alone, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"11692","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Harun ibn Idris al-Khushki narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When Umar embraced Islam, the people said: The people have taken their due from us."
"11693","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: {And when We directed to you a party of the jinn listening to the Qur'an; when they attended it}, the verse. He said: They were nine persons from the people of Nasibin, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made them messengers to their people."
"11694","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr informed us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The last funeral the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over, he said takbir over it four times."
"11695","Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Malik al-Fazari al-Kufi narrated to us: Abbad ibn Ya'qub al-Asadi narrated to us: al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: In the beginning of this ummah, their young learn from their elders, and at its end their elders learn from their young. It was said to Ibn Abbas: Why is that? He said: Because the young heard and the elders did not hear."
"11696","Ya'qub ibn Ghaylan narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be guarded; his uncle Abu Talib used to send with him every day men from Banu Hashim to guard him, until this verse was revealed, {O Messenger, convey what was revealed to you from your Lord}, up to His saying, {And Allah will protect you from people}. His uncle wanted to send someone with him to guard him, so he said: O my uncle, Allah Almighty has protected me from jinn and men."
"11697","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Azrah al-Shami narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us: al-Nadr Abu Umar narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted the testimony of a Bedouin for sighting the crescent of Ramadan."
"11698","Abu Shaykh Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asbahani narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us: Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Nadr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting and in ihram; a man called Abu Taybah cupped him, and he gave him his wage and interceded for him with his masters."
"11699","Abu Shaykh Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Shu'ayb ibn Ayyub al-Sarifini narrated to us: Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wala is for the one who frees."
"11700","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from al-Nadr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wala is for the one who frees."
"11701","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of what you change white hair with is henna and katam."
"11702","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Waki'i narrated to us: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Visiting the sick once is sunnah; what is more is supererogatory."
"11703","Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Sawrah al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us: My father narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized domestic donkeys on the day of Khaybar and cooked their meat. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the pots to be overturned, and forbade their meat that day."
"11704","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge, Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, all saying: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Zakariyya informed us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on Hira and the mountain shook. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be firm, O Hira, for there is upon you none but a prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr. And upon it were the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, Sad, and Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl."
"11705","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed after the Conquest seventeen days, praying two rakahs."
"11706","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us: Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in Asr as three rakahs, forgetting one. He left and entered upon one of his wives. A man of his Companions called Dhu al-Shimalayn entered upon him and said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened? He said: And what is that? He said: You prayed three. He took his hand and went out to people who were with him and said: Has Dhu al-Yadayn spoken the truth? They said: And what is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He claims that I prayed three. They said: He spoke the truth; we thought you were commanded in that with a command. So he led them in a rakah, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"11707","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abu Janab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sacrifice is obligatory upon me, and sunnah upon you."
"11708","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Jandal ibn Waliq narrated to us: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Asad ibn Ata, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should stand in a place where a man is killed unjustly, for the curse descends upon whoever is present when they did not defend him. And none of you should stand in a place where someone is beaten unjustly, for the curse descends upon whoever attends it when they did not defend him."
"11709","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Kudayr al-Kindi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions were swimming in a pond. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let every man of you swim to his companion. So every man of them swam to his companion, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr remained. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swam to Abu Bakr until he embraced him, and said: I am toward my companion, I am toward my companion."
"11710","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Isa ibn Qirtas narrated to us, who said: Ikrimah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray, raise your lower garments, for whatever of your lower garments touches the earth is in the Fire."
"11711","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Zayd Abu Usamah narrated to us: Ikrimah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed effeminate men, masculine women, the woman who tattoos and the woman who is tattooed, and the woman who joins hair and the woman who has it joined."
"11712","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari and Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn A'yan narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Junayd al-Hajjam narrated to us: Abu Usamah al-Hajjam narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer, nor does he drink wine while he is a believer, nor does he steal while he is a believer."
"11713","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Habib al-Tammar narrated to us, from Nizar ibn Hayyan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of denial of qadar, for it is a branch of Christianity."
"11714","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad al-Kufi, Humayd, and Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept until his snoring was heard, then stood and prayed, and did not perform ablution."
"11715","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us: Sallam ibn Abi Amrah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two groups of my ummah have no share in Islam: the Murji'ah and the Qadariyyah."
"11716","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Umar ibn Salit narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Hasirah narrated to us: Ikrimah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed mannish women and effeminate men."
"11717","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn Hanzalah ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit with his head bound with a soiled bandage. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: People increase and the Ansar decrease until they are among people like salt in food. Whoever of you is entrusted with a matter that benefits some people and harms others, let him accept from their good-doer and overlook their wrong-doer. He said: And it was the last sermon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave before he died."
"11718","Ahmad ibn Ma Bahram al-Idhaji narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Ismail ibn Musa ibn Uthman al-Ansari narrated to us, who said: I heard Sayfi ibn Rib'i narrating, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fasil, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah: Allah Almighty will not punish you, nor your children."
"11719","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bashir al-Kindi narrated to us: Amr ibn Atiyyah ibn al-Harith al-Wadi'i narrated to us, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day to his Companions: Whom do you count as martyrs among you? They said: One killed in the path of Allah, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating, is a martyr. He said: Then the martyrs of my ummah are few: One killed in the path of Allah is a martyr; a man who dies on his bed in the path of Allah is a martyr; one who dies of stomach illness is a martyr; one who is stung is a martyr; one who drowns is a martyr; one who chokes is a martyr; one devoured by a beast of prey is a martyr; one who falls from his mount is a martyr; the victim of a collapsing building is a martyr; the victim of pleurisy is a martyr; and a woman in childbed whom her child kills, dragging her with its cord to Paradise."
"11720","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Isa ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Allah never revealed: O you who believe, but Ali is its leader and its noble. Allah reproached the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in more than one place, and He mentioned Ali only with good."
"11721","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us: al-Musayyab ibn Sharik narrated to us, from Thabit Abu Hamzah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: When the women pledged not to display themselves with the display of the former Jahiliyyah, a woman said: O Messenger of Allah, I see you stipulate upon us not to display ourselves, yet so-and-so woman assisted me, and her brother has died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go and assist her, then come and pledge to me."
"11722","Uthman ibn Khalid ibn Amr al-Sulafi al-Himsi narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Ikrimah ibn Yazid al-Alhani narrated to us: al-Abyad ibn al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah narrated to me, from Abu Hamzah al-Thumali, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Zihar in Jahiliyyah made women unlawful. The first to declare zihar in Islam was Aws ibn al-Salt, and his wife was Khuwaylah bint Khuwaylid. The man was weak, and the woman was strong. When he uttered zihar, he said: I do not see you but that you have become unlawful to me. So go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); perhaps you will seek something that returns you to me. So she went, and he sat waiting for her at the two sides of the well. She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while a hairdresser was combing his head. She said: O Messenger of Allah, Aws ibn al-Samit, of whose weak judgment and incapable ability you know, has declared zihar upon me, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The most deserving to show good to him, if it be I, or to show good to me, if it be with him, yet he has declared zihar upon me, O Messenger of Allah. So seek something that returns me to him, may my father and mother be ransom for you. He said: O Khuwaylah, we have not been commanded anything concerning your affair, and if we are commanded I shall inform you. While his hairdresser had finished one side of his head and taken the other side, Allah Almighty sent down revelation. When revelation descended upon him, his face would redden for that until he felt its cold, then when it was lifted from him, his face returned white like the heart. Then he spoke with what he was commanded. His hairdresser said to her: O Khuwaylah, I think he is now concerned with your affair. She was seized by trembling, a shiver overcame her. Then she said: O Allah, in You I seek refuge from Your sending down concerning me anything but good, for I sought from Your Messenger nothing but good. When it was lifted from him, he said: O Khuwaylah, Allah has revealed concerning you and your companion: {Allah has heard the saying of her who disputes with you concerning her husband}, up to His saying, {then, those who return to what they said: freeing a slave before they touch one another}. She said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he has no servant but me, nor do I have a servant but him. He said: {Then whoever does not find: fasting two consecutive months}. She said: By Allah, if he does not eat twice a day, his sight dims. He said: {Then whoever is not able: feeding sixty poor}. She said: By Allah, we have for the day nothing but an uqiyyah. He said: Order him to go to so-and-so, take from him half a wasq of dates, give it in charity to sixty poor, and take you back. She said: So I came; when he saw me he said: What is behind you? She said: Good, though you are blameworthy: you are commanded to go to so-and-so, take from him half a wasq of dates, give it in charity to sixty poor, and take me back. So he went hastening until he brought it. She said: And my memory of him before that is that from weakness he could not carry on his back five sa's."
"11723","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us: Ali ibn Muhammad al-Tanafisi narrated to us: Mansur ibn Wardan al-Attar narrated to us: Abu Hamzah al-Thumali narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us in the Mosque of al-Khayf. He praised Allah and mentioned Him as He deserves, then said: Whoever's concern is the Hereafter, Allah gathers his affairs for him, places his sufficiency before his eyes, and the world comes to him humbled. Whoever's concern is the world, Allah scatters his affairs, places his poverty before his eyes, and nothing of the world comes to him except what was written."
"11724","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs wudu after ghusl is not of us."
"11725","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, from Bassam al-Sayrafi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jallalah sheep, the price of the dog, the stud fee of the stallion, and the earnings of the cupper."
"11726","Jabrun ibn Isa al-Muqri al-Misri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Hafari al-Qurashi narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of satiety in this world are the people of hunger in the Hereafter tomorrow."
"11727","Jabrun ibn Isa narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Hafari narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold to grief, for it is the key of the heart. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how is grief? He said: Hunger your souls with hunger and thirst them."
"11728","Jabrun ibn Isa al-Muqri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Hafari narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Musa ibn Imran passed by a man trembling, and he stood supplicating Allah for him to cure him. It was said to him: O Musa, what befalls him is not a share of Iblis, but he hungered himself for Me. He is the one who thinks that I look at him every day several times, marveling at his obedience to Me. So order him to supplicate for you, for he has every day an accepted supplication."
"11729","Jabrun ibn Isa al-Muqri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Hafari narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever angers Allah to please people, Allah is angry with him, and angers with him whoever he pleased in His anger. Whoever pleases Allah in the anger of people, Allah is pleased with him, and pleases with him whoever he angered in His pleasure, until He beautifies him and beautifies his word and deed in his eye."
"11730","Jabrun ibn Isa narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to his Companions one day with a piece of gold in his hand. He said to Abd Allah ibn Umar: What would Muhammad say to his Lord if he died while this was with him? Then he divided it before standing. Then he said: It would not please me that the Companions of Muhammad have like this mountain - and he pointed with his hand to Uhud - gold and silver, spending it in the path of Allah and leaving of it a dinar. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away on the day he passed away without leaving a dinar nor a dirham, nor a male nor a female slave. He left his armor pawned with a man of the Jews for thirty sa's of barley from which he ate and fed his family."
"11731","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ka'b narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I had intercourse with my wife while she was menstruating. So he ordered him to give half a dinar in charity."
"11732","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no harm in cupping for one fasting; it was disliked only because of weakness."
"11733","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi informed us: Abu Sa'd al-Baqqal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: {And We have given you seven of the oft-repeated}. He said: It is the Umm al-Kitab."
"11734","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Ya'ish narrated to us: Mus'ab ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Sa'd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Advise one another in knowledge, for the treachery of one of you in his knowledge is worse than his treachery in his wealth. And Allah Almighty will question you on the Day of Resurrection."
"11735","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Tha'labi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ya'la al-Aslami narrated to us, from Abu Sa'd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, is a town destroyed while righteous people are in it? He said: Yes. It was said: Why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Due to their laxity and silence toward disobedience of Allah."
"11736","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: While Safwan ibn Umayyah was sleeping in the mosque with his cloak under his head, a man came, slipped his cloak away and took it. He was brought with him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to be cut. He said: I did not think my cloak would cause the hand of a Muslim to be cut. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why not before you brought him?"
"11737","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from Madinah to Makkah and fasted until he reached Qudayd. He was brought a vessel of milk and broke his fast while on his mount, in Ramadan, and the people broke their fast. Those who broke their fast said to those who did not break: Break your fast, O disobedient ones."
"11738","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about a woman who vowed to perform Hajj walking. So he ordered her to perform Hajj riding."
"11739","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Salih ibn Ziyad al-Susi narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Tamim narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast before Ramadan; fast upon seeing it and break upon seeing it. If a cloud intervenes, complete thirty."
"11740","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, like the hadith before it, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tawaf between al-Safa and al-Marwah upon his mount."
"11741","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: {Those whom the angels take while wronging themselves; they say: In what were you? They say: We were weak in the earth. They say: Was not Allah's earth spacious that you might emigrate therein? Those, their abode is Hell, and evil as a destination}. They said: They were a people of Muslims in Makkah who went out with a people of polytheists in battle and were killed with them. Then this verse was revealed, {Except the weak among men, women, and children who can devise no plan nor find a way - those, perhaps Allah will pardon them}. So Allah excused those among them with excuse, and destroyed whoever had no excuse. Ibn Abbas said: And I and my mother were of those who had excuse."
"11742","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Damrah ibn Jundub left his house emigrating. He said to his family: Carry me and take me out of the land of polytheists to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He died on the way before reaching the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then revelation came down, {And whoever leaves his house emigrating to Allah and His Messenger}, until it reached, {And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful}."
"11743","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His Almighty saying, {And do not recite loudly in your prayer nor whisper it}. He said: When he supplicated he raised his voice."
"11744","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal and said: One-eyed, curly-haired, fair, bright, as if his head were a viper, most resembling among people Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan. But utter destruction is that he is one-eyed, while your Lord Almighty is not one-eyed."
"11745","Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Tammar and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Za'idah narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is curly-haired, fair, bright, as if his head were a tree branch, his left eye effaced and the other as if a floating grape, most resembling among people Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan. As for utter destruction, he is one-eyed, while your Lord is not one-eyed."
"11746","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is curly-haired, fair-skinned, bright white, as if his head were a tree branch, his left eye is effaced, and the other is as if it were a protruding grape; the person most resembling him is Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan; as for the doom of the doomed, he is one-eyed, and indeed your Lord is not one-eyed."
"11747","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that a wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed from janabah, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and performed ablution from her leftover water, so she said: I bathed from it, and he said: Nothing makes water impure."
"11748","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to bathe one day, so a wife of his said: O Messenger of Allah, it is the remainder of a bath. He said: Water does not become impure."
"11749","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: One of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed in a large bowl, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to perform ablution from it or to bathe, so she said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I was in janabah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water does not become impure."
"11750","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nuaym, narrated to us Sufyan, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, who said: Ibn Abbas passed by people who had set up a pigeon as a target shooting at it, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking a living soul as a target."
"11751","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad, narrated to us Asbat ibn Nasr, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he passed by people who had set up a pigeon and were shooting at it, so he said: Do not take a living soul as a target."
"11752","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people of the Ansar who had set up a pigeon shooting at it, so he said: Do not take anything with a soul as a target."
"11753","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih al-Ijli, narrated to us Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning this verse: O you who believe, indeed among your wives and your children are enemies to you, so beware of them: he said: These were men of the people of Makkah who accepted Islam and wanted to come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then when they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and gained understanding in religion, they wanted to punish them, so Allah Almighty revealed: O you who believe, indeed among your wives and your children are enemies to you, so beware of them; but if you pardon and overlook and forgive, then indeed Allah is Forgiving, Merciful."
"11754","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A woman accepted Islam in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then her first husband came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I accepted Islam along with her and she knew of my Islam along with her; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took her from her latter husband and returned her to her first husband."
"11755","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih al-Ijli, narrated to us Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning: while you amuse yourselves: he said: Heedless, turning away from it."
"11756","Narrated to us Abu Man Thabit ibn Nuaym al-Hawji, narrated to us Adam ibn Abi Iyas (ha). And narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us Khalaf ibn al-Walid, both saying: narrated to us Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The prophets were from the Children of Israel except ten: Nuh and Hud and Lut and Shuayb and Ibrahim and Ismail and Ishaq and Isa and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and upon them all; and there is no prophet who has al-jaddah: two names, except Isa and Yaqub, peace be upon them both."
"11757","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani, narrated to us Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali, narrated to us Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the beards full and trim the mustaches. He said: And Ibrahim, peace be upon him, the close friend of the Most Merciful, used to leave his beard full and trim his mustache."
"11758","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj, narrated to us Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Salih and Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to trim his mustache, and that Ibrahim the close friend used to trim his mustache."
"11759","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nuaym, narrated to us Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that one-fifth is due on buried treasure."
"11760","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us Khalaf ibn al-Walid, narrated to us Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The righteous dream is one part of seventy parts of prophethood."
"11761","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us Khalaf ibn al-Walid, narrated to us Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man should not touch another man skin to skin, nor a woman another woman."
"11762","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, narrated to us Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, what about those who died while praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis? So Allah Almighty revealed: And Allah would never let your faith go to waste; indeed Allah is Kind, Merciful to people."
"11763","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, narrated to us Israil, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the prohibition of wine was revealed they said: O Messenger of Allah, those who died while drinking wine? So there was revealed: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted. The verse."
"11764","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi (ha), and narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us Khalaf ibn al-Walid, both saying: narrated to us Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man of Banu Sulaym passed by a group of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with sheep with him, and he greeted them, so they said: He only greeted you to protect himself; so they set upon him and killed him and took his sheep, and brought them to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so Allah Almighty revealed: O you who believe, when you go forth in the way of Allah, verify. Up to His saying: You were like that before."
"11765","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, narrated to us Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: Our Lord, we believe, so write us among the witnesses: he said: With Muhammad and his ummah, for they bore witness that he conveyed, and they bore witness for the man that they conveyed."
"11766","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, narrated to us Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he finished Badr: Go for the caravan, there is nothing beyond it; so al-Abbas, while a captive in bonds, said: That is not right; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why? He said: Because Allah promised you one of the two parties, and He has given you what He promised you."
"11767","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad (ha), and narrated to us Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri, narrated to us Yusuf ibn Adi, both saying: narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, narrated to us Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People of my ummah will recite the Quran, passing out of Islam as the arrow passes through the game."
"11768","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad (ha). And narrated to us Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri, narrated to us Yusuf ibn Adi, both saying: narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, narrated to us Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to set out on a journey he would say: O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over the family; O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the burden of travel and gloom on return; O Allah, fold up the land for us and make travel easy for us. And when he returned he would say: Returning, repenting, worshipping, praising our Lord. And when he entered upon his family he would say: Return, return; to our Lord is repentance; leaving no sin."
"11769","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas and Ali ibn Said al-Raziyan, both saying: narrated to us Abd al-Mumin ibn Ali, narrated to us Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds a wall, let him support it upon the wall of his brother."
"11770","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas and Ali ibn Said al-Raziyan, both saying: narrated to us Abd al-Mumin ibn Ali, narrated to us Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you differ over the road, make it seven cubits, and do not make it less than that."
"11771","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Said al-Asbahani, narrated to us Sharik, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a well-cooked shoulder of a young camel, he says: mature; and he wiped his hand with a cloth and prayed."
"11772","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder, then wiped his hand with a cloth that was beneath him, then stood and prayed."
"11773","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nuaym, narrated to us Sharik, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas; it was said to Sharik: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. He said: There is no alliance in Islam, and every alliance in the Jahiliyyah, Islam only increased it in severity and strictness."
"11774","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani, narrated to us Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Salih and Sharik, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: When you prostrate, press your hands to the ground; Sharik added: for you were commanded to do that."
"11775","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti, narrated to us Sharik, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, I shall surely raid Quraysh; by Allah, I shall surely raid Quraysh. Then he said the third time: If Allah wills."
"11776","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib and Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani, both saying: narrated to us Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti, narrated to us Sharik, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a caravan that had come with ounces of gold, and gave it in charity to the widows of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, and said: I do not buy anything for which I do not have its price."
"11777","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Abdan ibn Ahmad, both saying: narrated to us Tamim ibn al-Muntasir, narrated to us Ishaq al-Azraq, from Sharik, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Aishah bought Barirah from the Ansar to free her, and they stipulated her wala for themselves, so she stipulated that for them; when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came she told him, so he said: Wala belongs only to the one who frees. Then he ascended the minbar and said: What is with people who stipulate conditions not in the Book of Allah? Whatever condition is not in the Book of Allah is rejected back to the Book of Allah. And Barirah had a husband, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice whether to remain with her husband as she was or to part from him, so she parted from him; then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and saw a sheep's trotter, so he said to Aishah: Will you not cook this meat for us? She said: It was given in charity to Barirah, and she gifted it to us. He said: Cook it, for it is charity for her and a gift for us."
"11778","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Hisham ibn Ammar, narrated to us Hammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed effeminate men and said: Expel them from your houses."
"11779","Narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud Abu Dawud, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Muadh, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Sawdah feared that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would divorce her, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, keep me and do not divorce me, and give my day to Aishah; so he did, and Allah Almighty revealed: There is no blame upon them if they make terms of settlement between them, and settlement is best; so whatever they settle upon of anything is permissible."
"11780","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani and Yusuf al-Qadi, both saying: narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Muadh, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Abdullah ibn Ubayy had a slave girl who committed adultery in the Jahiliyyah; when adultery was prohibited, he said: Will you not commit adultery? She said: No, by Allah, I will never commit adultery; so there was revealed: And do not compel your slave girls to prostitution."
"11781","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, both saying: narrated to us Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, narrated to us Abu Dawud, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Muadh, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between his companions, so they used to inherit from one another for that reason, until there was revealed: And blood relatives are more entitled to one another; so they inherited by kinship."
"11782","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, narrated to us Abu Dawud, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Muadh, narrated to us Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted while traveling and broke his fast."
"11783","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us my uncle al-Qasim, narrated to us Yahya ibn Yala, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Hand me a handful of pebbles; so he handed him, and he threw them at the faces of the people, and no one of the people remained except his eyes were filled with pebbles; so there was revealed: And you did not throw when you threw, but Allah threw."
"11784","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us Muawiyah ibn Amr, narrated to us Zaidah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and those with him prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months, then the qiblah was changed afterwards."
"11785","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us Muawiyah ibn Amr, narrated to us Zaidah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon a small mat."
"11786","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad, narrated to us Asbat ibn Nasr, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he used to pray upon a mat."
"11787","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us Muawiyah ibn Amr, narrated to us Zaidah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it; if a cloud barrier comes between you and it, complete the number, and the month is twenty-nine."
"11788","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Asadi, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not precede the month; fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it; if there is a cloud barrier between you and it, complete the number."
"11789","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast before Ramadan; fast upon seeing it, and if a cloud barrier comes between you and it, complete thirty."
"11790","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not anticipate the month; fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it, and if a cloud barrier comes between you and it, complete the number."
"11791","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad (ha). And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar, narrated to us Musa ibn Ismail, both saying: narrated to us Abu Awanah, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began speaking eloquent speech, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some eloquence is magic, and indeed some poetry is wisdom."
"11792","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami al-Misri, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, narrated to us Man ibn Isa, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some poetry is wisdom."
"11793","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan, narrated to us Abbad ibn Abbad, from Shubah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some poetry is wisdom."
"11794","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami al-Misri, narrated to us Yusuf ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar, narrated to us Sharik, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - raised it - who said: Indeed some poetry is wisdom, and some eloquence is magic."
"11795","Narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, narrated to us Abu Kamil al-Jahdari, narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Kufi, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some poetry is wisdom."
"11796","Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, who said: I said to Abu Usamah: Did Zaidah narrate to you, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed some poetry is wisdom, and indeed some eloquence is magic; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to quote verses of poetry? He said: Yes."
"11797","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad (ha). And narrated to us Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani, narrated to us Ibn al-Tabba, both saying: narrated to us Abu Awanah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no contagion, no evil omen, no hamah, and no Safar. So a man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, we take a mangy sheep and cast it among the flock and they become mangy. He said: Then who infected the first?"
"11798","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Abu Awanah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A sheep of Sawdah bint Zamah died, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has died - meaning the sheep - so he said: Why did you not take its skin? They said: Do we take the skin of a sheep that died? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: He only said: Say: I find not in what was revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats it except carrion or outpoured blood or the flesh of swine; you would not eat it, you would only tan it and benefit from it. So she sent for it and skinned it and tanned it, and made a waterskin from it until it wore out with her."
"11799","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A sheep of Umm al-Aswad died, so she told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: I find not in what was revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats it except carrion or blood; to the end of the verse; and he said: You would not eat it; so she sent for it and skinned it. Ibn Abbas said: So they made its skin a waterskin which I saw after a year. Abu al-Ahwas said: Umm al-Aswad, though the correct one is Sawdah."
"11800","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad, narrated to us Asbat ibn Nasr, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, who said: There were two co-wives, and there was noisy quarreling between them, so one of them threw a stone at the other, and she miscarried a dead boy, and the woman died; so he ruled blood money upon the aqilah. So her uncle said: She miscarried, O Messenger of Allah, a boy whose hair had grown. So the father of the killer said: He lies; by Allah, it neither cried at birth, nor reasoned, nor drank, nor ate, so the like of it goes uncompensated. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rhymed speech of the Jahiliyyah and its soothsaying? I see a ghurrah for the boy. Ibn Abbas said: The name of one of them was Mulaykah, and the other Umm Utayf."
"11801","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Amr ibn Hammad, narrated to us Asbat ibn Nasr, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram."
"11802","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari, narrated to us Muawiyah ibn Amr, narrated to us Zaidah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Avoid drinking from gourds, hantams, and muzaffat; drink from skins, and if you fear its fermentation then dilute it with water."
"11803","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Husayn ibn Ali, from Zaidah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A cooked dabb lizard was gifted to one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she sent it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the people ate, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not eat; so Khalid ibn al-Walid said: O Messenger of Allah, is it unlawful so we leave it? He said: No, but I find it distasteful."
"11804","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Asadi, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A dabb lizard was gifted to one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she sent it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the people ate, other than the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so Khalid ibn al-Walid said: Is it unlawful, O Messenger of Allah, so we leave it? He said: No, but I find it distasteful."
"11805","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Abu Usamah, from Ali ibn Salih, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: Forbidden to you are your mothers. He said: Seven are forbidden to you by lineage and seven by marriage; and His saying: And lawful to you is what is beyond that: he said: By lineage; and His saying: The decree of Allah upon you: he said: Four."
"11806","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Sharik, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Ali, so he prepared ghusl water for him, then gave him a garment and said: Cover me and turn your back to me."
"11807","Narrated to us Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali (ha), and narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, both saying: narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not go out to meet the market, do not leave milk in the udder to deceive, and let none of you outbid for another."
"11808","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People of my ummah will recite the Quran, passing out of Islam as the arrow passes through the game."
"11809","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Hawwas al-Hanafi, narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning the saying of Allah Almighty: And stand before Allah devoutly. He said: They used to speak in prayer; a man's servant would come to him while he was in prayer and speak to him about his need, so they were forbidden from speech."
"11810","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad (ha), and narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mundhir al-Qazzaz, Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar, and Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini, who said: narrated to us Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was sleeping and I was visited, and it was said to me: Tonight is Laylat al-Qadr; so I rose while drowsy, and my foot caught on one of the ropes of the tent of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was standing praying. Ibn Abbas said: So I looked at the night and it was the night of the twenty-third. And the wording is from the hadith of Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi."
"11811","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Masruq ibn al-Marzuban, narrated to us Ibn Abi Zaidah, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It would not please me to have red camels if I broke the alliance that was in Dar al-Nadwah."
"11812","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani, narrated to us Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The slaughtered animals of the Jews and Christians were only permitted because they believed in the Torah and the Gospel."
"11813","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr, narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, informed us Sharik, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has land and wants to sell it, let him offer it to his neighbor."
"11814","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan, narrated to us Fihr, from Umar ibn Musa ibn Wajih, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not prohibit leasing land, but he commanded noble morals."
"11815","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi, narrated to us Sahl ibn Mahmud, narrated to us Salih ibn Umar, from Hatim ibn Abi Saghairah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever abandons a prayer meets Allah while He is angry with him."
"11816","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Said al-Basri, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah al-Dashtaki, narrated to us Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade buying fruit until it is edible."
"11817","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Hisham al-Rifai, narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Hubab, from Abu Awanah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I was aided by al-saba wind, and Ad were destroyed by al-dabur wind."
"11818","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me Abu Musa al-Harawi, narrated to us Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad, narrated to us Husayn and Hazim ibn Ibrahim, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to prostrate upon a cloth. And Husayn means al-Muallim."
"11819","Narrated to us Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us Hazim ibn Ibrahim, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: People disputed over the crescent in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so a Bedouin came and testified that he saw it; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal, who announced: Fasting is tomorrow."
"11820","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Kufi, narrated to us Yunus ibn Bukayr, from Anbasah ibn al-Azhar, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had no woman who offered herself to him."
"11821","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati, narrated to us Fudayl ibn Abd al-Wahhab, narrated to us Amr ibn Thabit, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: They were merchants whom neither trade nor sale diverted from the remembrance of Allah."
"11822","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Sijistani, narrated to us Yahya ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade blowing into food, drink, and fruit."
"11823","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bazzah, narrated to us Muammal ibn Ismail, narrated to us Sufyan, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not revile Tubba, for he had accepted Islam."
"11824","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Missisi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon every joint of a person is a charity each day. So some of the people said: This is hard, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Enjoining good and forbidding evil is a charity, carrying for the weak is a charity, and every step one of you takes toward prayer is a charity."
"11825","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Musa ibn Abi Uthman al-Anmati, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah, narrated to us Harami ibn Umarah, narrated to us Hazim ibn Ibrahim Abu Muhammad al-Kufi, narrated to us Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Muslim owes a charity, and every step one of you takes toward prayer is a charity."
"11826","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari, both saying: narrated to us Mualla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili, narrated to us Abu Awanah, from Abu Yunus, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that a man of Banu Abs called Khalid ibn Sinan said to his people: I shall extinguish for you the fire of al-hadathan. Umarah ibn Ziyad, a man of his people, said to him: By Allah, you never told us, O Khalid, anything but truth, so what is your affair with the fire of al-hadathan? You claim you will extinguish it? So Umarah ibn Ziyad went with him along with people of his people until they came to it, emerging from a mountain cleft in a lava field called Harrat Ashja. Khalid drew a line for them and seated them in it, and said: If I am late returning to you, do not call me by my name. It came out as if blond horses following one another, so Khalid faced it striking it with his staff while saying: Appear, appear; all guidance rejected; the son of the goatherdess claims I shall not come out of it with my clothes damp; until he entered the cleft with it, and was late returning to them. Umarah ibn Ziyad said: By Allah, had your companion been alive he would have come out to you by now. They said: He forbade us to call him by his name. So they called him by his name, and he came out to them holding his head, and said: Did I not forbid you to call me by my name? By Allah, you have killed me; so bury me, and when donkeys pass by you among them a docked donkey, exhume me, for you will find me alive. Donkeys passed by them among them a docked donkey, so they said: Exhume him, for he commanded us to exhume him; but Umarah ibn Ziyad said to them: Mudar must not say we exhume our dead; by Allah, you shall never exhume him. Khalid had told them that in his wife's saddlebag were two tablets; when a matter perplexes you, look into them, for you will see what you ask about; and he said: No menstruating woman should touch them. When they returned to his wife they asked her about them, so she brought them out while menstruating, and the knowledge in them vanished. Abu Yunus said: Simak said: The son of Khalid ibn Sinan came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Welcome to the son of my brother. And Abu Yunus is Hatim ibn Abi Saghairah."
"11827","Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us Abu Muawiyah, from al-Shaybani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man touching another man skin to skin, and a woman another woman."
"11828","Narrated to us Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad (ha). And narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Rahawayh (ha), and narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Salt Abu Yala al-Thawri, all saying: narrated to us Abu Muawiyah, from al-Shaybani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah. And Ikrimah used to dislike selling qasil."
"11829","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us Sharik, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten of Ramadan."
"11830","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Nusayr ibn Dhuluq, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a coat of mail pawned with a Jew, and he found nothing to redeem it with until he died."
"11831","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Ubayd ibn Yaish, narrated to us Yunus ibn Bukayr, informed us Matar ibn Maymun, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man of his companions to a man of the Jews to kill him, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to speak; so he said: Say whatever occurs to you, for war is deception."
"11832","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer. Ikrimah said: So I said to Ibn Abbas: How is faith removed? He said: Like this; and he described interlacing his fingers then taking them out; then if he repents it returns to that."
"11833","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, both saying: narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us Yahya ibn Yala, from Musa ibn Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a slave whom his master marries off: In whose hand is divorce? He said: In the hand of the one who took hold of the leg."
"11834","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Numayr, from Musa ibn Muslim, who said: I heard Ikrimah raising the hadith, as I see, to Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves snakes out of fear of seeking them is not of us."
"11835","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail, narrated to us Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sacrifice and slaughter were prescribed upon me but not prescribed upon you, and I was commanded to pray Duha but you were not commanded to do it."
"11836","Narrated to us Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti, narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh, narrated to us Sharik, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, raised it, who said: Sacrifice was prescribed upon me but not prescribed upon you, and I was commanded to pray Duha but you were not commanded to do it."
"11837","Narrated to us Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi, narrated to us Qabisah ibn Uqbah, narrated to us Sufyan, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to a village four or two farsakhs away on the day of Ashura: Whoever has not eaten, let him complete his fast, and whoever ate, let him not eat the rest of his day."
"11838","Narrated to us Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri, narrated to us Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruwasi, narrated to us Musab ibn Mahan, narrated to us Sufyan, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman should not be married along with her paternal aunt, nor along with her maternal aunt."
"11839","Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani, narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Thawr, from Mamar, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No harm and no reciprocating harm; a man may place a beam upon his neighbor's wall; and when you doubt over the road, make it seven cubits."
"11840","Narrated to us Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti, narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh (ha), and narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, both saying: narrated to us Sharik and Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought cheese during the campaign of Taif, and his companions began striking it with their sticks saying: We fear it may contain carrion; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put the knife in it and mention the name of Allah over it."
"11841","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi, narrated to us Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, narrated to us Zuhayr, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not enter the House during Hajj, but entered in the year of the Conquest; when he came down he prayed four rakahs, or he said: two rakahs, between the Stone and the Door facing the House, and said: This is the qiblah."
"11842","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jaban, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Hammal, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Musa, from Israil, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed three and gave salam, so Dhu al-Shimalayn said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is it as Dhu al-Yadayn says? He said: Yes; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed one rakah and prostrated two prostrations."
"11843","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn al-Abbas al-Razi, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abi Surayj al-Razi, narrated to us Ali ibn Hafs al-Madaini, narrated to us Ubayd al-Muktib al-Kufi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no believing servant but he has a sin he returns to time after time, or a sin he persists in never leaving until he departs; the believer was created tested, oft-repenting, forgetful; when reminded he remembers."
"11844","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me Dawud ibn Rushayd, narrated to us Marwan ibn Muawiyah, narrated to us Malik ibn al-Husayn, from Ubayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When a noble man of a people comes to you, honor him."
"11845","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, narrated to us Sharik, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: He only said: Water is from water, concerning nocturnal emission."
"11846","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nuaym, narrated to us Sufyan, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Prayer of one for another is not fitting, except upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11847","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn al-Zibriqan al-Kufi, narrated to us Asbat ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi, from al-Amash, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had raisin nabidh; he would drink it that day and the next, and when it was the third he drank it, otherwise he poured it out."
"11848","Narrated to us Ubayd al-Ijli, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakkar, narrated to us Adi ibn al-Fadl, from Abu Ishaq, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear his ring on his right."
"11849","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Alawiyyah al-Qattan, narrated to us Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar, narrated to us Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan, from Abu Sufyan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sponsors an orphan, his own or another's, Paradise becomes due for him, unless he did a deed that is not forgiven; and whoever loses his two precious ones, Paradise becomes due for him, unless he did a deed that is not forgiven. Abu Sufyan, in my view, is Said ibn Masruq, and Allah knows best."
"11850","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Marwan al-Wasiti, narrated to us Wahb ibn Baqiyyah, informed us Ali ibn Asim, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) singled us out with three things only: to perfect ablution, not to eat charity, and not to breed donkeys upon horses."
"11851","Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab, narrated to us Isa ibn Muslim al-Hamdani, narrated to us Maysarah ibn Ammar al-Ashjai, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with Khadijah, Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: O Muhammad, convey my salam to Khadijah, and give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, with no pain in it and no toil."
"11852","Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, both saying: narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mujaththamah and jallalah, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"11853","Narrated to us al-Sari ibn Sahl al-Jundaysaburi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Rashid, narrated to us Mujjaah ibn al-Zubayr, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mujaththamah and jallalah, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"11854","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Muadh ibn Hisham, narrated to me my father, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin, and mujaththamah, and the milk of jallalah."
"11855","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Said ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that his days of life be lengthened and his provision increased, let him uphold his kinship."
"11856","Narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi, both saying: narrated to us Amr ibn Marzuq, informed us Shubah, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed men who imitate women and women who imitate men."
"11857","Narrated to us Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali, narrated to us Shubah, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: This and this are equal. Meaning: the thumb and the little finger, their blood money is equal."
"11858","Narrated to us Uthman ibn Umar, narrated to us Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, narrated to us Shubah, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The husband of Barirah was a slave."
"11859","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Hudbah ibn Khalid, narrated to us Hammam, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The husband of Barirah was a black slave called Mughith. Ibn Abbas said: I used to see him in the streets of Madinah squeezing his eyes; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled four things concerning her: her masters stipulated wala upon her, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that wala belongs to the one who frees; he gave her the choice and she chose herself; he commanded her to observe waiting period; charity was given to her and she gifted some of it to Aishah; so Aishah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"11860","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, both saying: narrated to us Hudbah ibn Khalid, narrated to us Hammam, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tawaf seven times then performed sai, because he loved to show people his strength."
"11861","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz, narrated to us Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi (ha), and narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, narrated to us Hudbah ibn Khalid, both saying: narrated to us Hammam, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that Uqbah ibn Amir came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: His sister vowed to walk to the House; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is free of need of your sister's vow; let her ride and offer a sacrificial camel."
"11862","Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the sister of Uqbah ibn Amir vowed to walk; he mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"11863","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani, narrated to us Shayban ibn Farrukh, narrated to us Hammam, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: Mankind were one community: he said: Upon Islam."
"11864","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Najiyah and Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti, both saying: narrated to us Qasim ibn Isa al-Tai (ha), and narrated to us Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Wasiti, both saying: narrated to us Talhah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever makes an image will be burdened on the Day of Resurrection to breathe the soul into it; whoever listens to the speech of people who dislike it, molten lead will be poured into his ear; and whoever falsely claims a dream will be burdened to tie a knot between two barley grains."
"11865","Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Wasiti, narrated to us Talhah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: I saw at al-Abtah a foolish old man who says takbir when he prostrates and when he raises his head. He said: Is that not the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may you have no mother?"
"11866","Narrated to us Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Yazid ibn Zuray, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah bint al-Harith while in ihram, and consummated with her after he returned at a water called Sarif."
"11867","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri, narrated to us Abd al-Ala, narrated to us Said, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that Jamilah bint Salul came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I find no fault with Thabit ibn Qays in character or religion, but I cannot bear him, and I dislike disbelief in Islam; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you return his garden to him? She said: Yes; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to take from her what he had given her and not increase."
"11868","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari, narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Qurashi, narrated to us Abbad ibn al-Awwam, narrated to us Said, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever changes his religion, kill him."
"11869","Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Muadh ibn Hisham, narrated to me my father, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, my father is a very old sick man; standing is hard for me, so command me a night in which Allah may grant me Laylat al-Qadr. He said: Take the seventh."
"11870","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me Bahz ibn Asad, narrated to us Hammam, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade Abd al-Qays from muzza, and I fear it is busr."
"11871","Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Hafs, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Tahman, narrated to me al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"11872","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani, narrated to us Uthman ibn Talut, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bilal, narrated to us Imran ibn al-Qattan, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Quran was sent down on Laylat al-Qadr in Ramadan to the lowest heaven all at once, then it was sent down in portions."
"11873","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bilal, narrated to us Imran al-Qattan, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made two rakahs obligatory in travel, as he made four obligatory in residence."
"11874","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd al-Bazzaz al-Baghdadi, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami, from Shayban, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When there was revealed: O Prophet, indeed We sent you as a witness, a bearer of glad tidings, and a warner; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ali and Muadh, and he had commanded them to go out to Yemen, and said: Go and give glad tidings, do not repel, make easy and do not make hard; for there was revealed to me: O Prophet, indeed We sent you as a witness; upon your ummah, a bearer of glad tidings of Paradise, a warner of the Fire, a caller to the testimony that there is no god but Allah, and an illuminating lamp by the Quran."
"11875","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Malik al-Fazari al-Kufi, both saying: narrated to us Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Asadi, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami, from Shayban, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his face dripping blood, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I followed a woman, then a man met me and did to me what you see; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends good for a servant He hastens the punishment of his sin in this world, and when He intends evil for a servant He withholds his sin until he meets it on the Day of Resurrection as if a mountain donkey."
"11876","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Ishaq al-Anmati, narrated to us Hisham ibn Ammar, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Muslim, narrated to us Shayban, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I saw the Dajjal, bright white, fair, huge, elephantine, as if the hair of his head were tree branches, one-eyed, as if his eye were the morning star; I liken him to Abd al-Uzza, a man of Khuzaah."
"11877","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi, narrated to us Amr ibn Makhlad al-Laythi, narrated to us Asim ibn Hilal al-Bariqi, narrated to us Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn the two radiant ones: al-Baqarah and Al Imran; for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if two clouds, or as if two shades, or as if two flocks of birds in ranks arguing on behalf of their companion. Learn al-Baqarah, for taking it is blessing and leaving it is regret, and the sorcerers cannot handle it."
"11878","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, informed us Abd al-Razzaq, informed us Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw images in the House, meaning the Kabah, he did not enter until he ordered them effaced; and he saw Ibrahim and Ismail with divining arrows in their hands, so he said: May Allah destroy them; by Allah, they never sought division by arrows."
"11879","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I only know that he raised the hadith: that he used to command killing snakes, and said: Whoever leaves them out of fear or dread of revenge is not of us. Ibn Abbas said: Snakes are transformed jinn, as monkeys were transformed from the Children of Israel."
"11880","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, informed us Abd al-Razzaq, informed us Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir and Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed effeminate men and masculine women."
"11881","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed effeminate men and masculine women."
"11882","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I attended Eid with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he addressed, then thought he had not made the women hear, so he came to them and admonished them and said: Give charity. So the woman began casting her ring, earring, ornaments, and other things; then he commanded Bilal who gathered it in his garments until he carried it off."
"11883","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever changes his religion - or he said: returns from his religion - kill him. And he said: Do not punish with the punishment of Allah, meaning the Fire."
"11884","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, informed us Abd al-Razzaq, informed us Ibn Jurayj and Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the husband of Barirah was a slave of Banu so-and-so, people of the Ansar, called Mughith; by Allah, I can still see him now following her in the streets of Madinah while weeping."
"11885","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have no evil example; one who takes back his gift is like a dog returning to its vomit."
"11886","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq (ha), and narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nuaym, both from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who takes back his gift is like a dog returning to its vomit; we have no evil example."
"11887","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, who said: I heard Ikrimah narrating from Ibn Abbas, who said: It is not abrogated; he used to read it (they shall be encircled): it concerns the very old man who is burdened with fasting but cannot bear it, so he breaks fast and feeds."
"11888","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, informed us Abd al-Razzaq, informed us Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, I only know from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever makes an image will be burdened on the Day of Resurrection to breathe the soul into it, and he will never breathe; he will be punished for it; whoever listens to the speech of people who dislike it, molten lead will be poured into his earhole; and whoever lies about his dream will be burdened to tie a barley grain - or he said: between two barley grains - and punished for that, and he will never do it."
"11889","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Mamar al-Muqad, narrated to us Abd al-Warith, narrated to us Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed aqiqah for al-Hasan with a ram and for al-Husayn with a ram."
"11890","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muadh al-Halabi, narrated to us Musa ibn Ismail, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the mukatab dies leaving inheritance, or commits a hadd offense, he inherits in proportion to what was freed of him, and the hadd is applied to him in proportion to what was freed of him."
"11891","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about Laylat al-Qadr, he said: Seek it in the ninth night remaining, and in the seventh remaining, and in the fifth remaining."
"11892","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: had cupping done while he was in ihram."
"11893","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: had cupping done while he was fasting."
"11894","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not boast about your forefathers who passed away in the pre-Islamic ignorance, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the dung that the dung beetle rolls with its nose is better than them."
"11895","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not boast about your forefathers who died in the pre-Islamic ignorance, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, what the dung beetle rolls with its nose is better than your forefathers who died in the pre-Islamic ignorance."
"11896","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: married Maymunah while he was in ihram, and consummated the marriage with her at Sarif while he was out of ihram."
"11897","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrating in Surah Sad, and it is not among the obligatory prostrations."
"11898","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrating in Surah Sad."
"11899","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Juddi narrated to us, and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Mihran al-Sammak narrated to us, both saying: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: prostrated while in Makkah at Surah al-Najm, and the Muslims, the polytheists, the jinn and mankind prostrated with him; and Hafs ibn Umar said in his hadith: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrated in Makkah, and the Jews, the Christians and the polytheists prostrated with him."
"11900","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ruzzi narrated to us, Asim ibn Hilal al-Bariqi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Safiyyah menstruated after she had performed the tawaf, so Aishah said to her: Are you in loss? I see you will detain us; so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is that? Safiyyah said: She has menstruated; it was said: She has already performed the tawaf al-ifadah; he said: Then no harm, so depart."
"11901","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Qazah narrated to us, Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: used to take from the heads while fasting, meaning: the kiss."
"11902","Al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Natta narrated to us, and Yahya ibn Muadh al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hafs al-Tumani narrated to us, Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had cupping done and paid its wage, and had it been impure he would not have fed him from it."
"11903","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before stoning; so he gestured with his hand and said: No harm; and on that day he was not asked about anything regarding doing things earlier or later except he gestured with his hand and said: No harm."
"11904","Al-Sari ibn Sahl al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Rashid narrated to us, Mujjaah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man known as Abu Israil vowed not to speak, not to seek shade, not to sit, and to fast his day; so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Command him to speak, to seek shade, to sit, and to fast his day."
"11905","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on a journey when he passed by a woman with her hair uncovered, so he said: What is this? It was said: So-and-so, a woman of Quraysh, vowed to perform Hajj with her hair uncovered; he said: Command her to cover her head with a khimar."
"11906","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Shadh ibn al-Fayyad narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Between the Corner and the Maqam there is the Multazam; no afflicted person supplicates there except he is cured."
"11907","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib al-Taraifi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Hayyan, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: passed by a woman with her hair uncovered, and he mentioned the hadith."
"11908","Abdan ibn Ahmad and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, both saying: al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us, Said ibn Sufyan al-Jahdari narrated to us, Said ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Hayyah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a group came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bringing with them a woman, and they said: O Muhammad, what was revealed to you about adultery? He said: Go and bring me two men from the scholars of the Children of Israel; so they brought him two men, one a young eloquent man, and the other a young man whose eyebrows had fallen over his eyes so that he lifted them with a headband; so he said: I adjure you by Allah to inform me of what Allah revealed to Musa about the adulterer; they said: You have adjured us by something great, and we inform you that Allah revealed to Musa about the adulterer: stoning; and we were a youthful people, and our women were beautiful-faced, and that became widespread among us, and we could not uphold it, so we resorted to flogging and public disgrace; so he said: Take your woman away, and when she delivers what is in her womb, then stone her."
"11909","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to a people who had set up a live dove as a target and were shooting at it, so he said: This tied-up living target, eating it is not lawful."
"11910","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, al-Yaman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: used to drink from the vessel in three breaths."
"11911","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Yaman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Everything of the lower garment that goes below the ankles is in the Fire."
"11912","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Yaman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: would not blow into the drink."
"11913","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Dharra narrated to us, Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Exalted is He, loves that His concessions be acted upon just as He loves that His strict obligations be acted upon."
"11914","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Qalusi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Zakariyya al-Suraymi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Exalted is He, loves that His strict obligations be acted upon."
"11915","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Qalusi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Zakariyya al-Suraymi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the overwhelming of debt and the overwhelming of the enemy, and from the ruin of the widow without husband, and from the trial of the Dajjal."
"11916","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi ibn Shahin and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, both saying: Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When Hilal ibn Umayyah accused his wife with Sharik ibn al-Sahma, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: You must bring proof for what you say, or you will be flogged with the prescribed punishment; he said: By the One Who sent you with the truth, I am truthful, and Allah will surely send down my vindication; then the verse of mutual cursing came down, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called him and they performed the mutual cursing; and when the fifth one remained, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is decisive, and I wanted her to be shown mercy; then she said: By Allah, I will not disgrace my people, and she went ahead; so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Watch her; if she brings him white, lank-haired, short-eyed, then he belongs to Hilal ibn Umayyah, and if she brings him dark, curly-haired, black-eyed, then he belongs to Sharik ibn al-Sahma; so she brought him belonging to Sharik."
"11917","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Maymun narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever listens to the talk of a people, molten lead will be poured into his ear, and whoever claims a false dream will be charged with tying two grains of barley together and he will not be able to tie them."
"11918","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the husband of Barirah was a slave, and I saw him striking his head against the walls in seeking her."
"11919","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn al-Rabi ibn Abi Rashid narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Concession was granted regarding drinking from the mouths of waterskins."
"11920","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I did not pass by any company of angels except they commanded me with cupping."
"11921","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to apply antimony kohl before sleeping every night."
"11922","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: When revelation was sent down upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, it weighed heavily upon him, and the people refrained from speaking to him."
"11923","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when the first dawn rose, he stood and prayed witr with nine rakahs, giving salams between every two rakahs."
"11924","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, Asram ibn Hawshab narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever spends a night in lightness of food and drink, praying, the wide-eyed houris crowd around him until morning."
"11925","Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Waki ibn Muhriz narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: stayed in Makkah seventeen days shortening the prayer."
"11926","Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Waki ibn Muhriz narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of servants is the cupper: he removes the blood, lightens the back, and brightens the sight."
"11927","Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: a red velvet cloth was placed in his grave."
"11928","Ibrahim ibn Nailah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: had cupping done while he was fasting."
"11929","Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: sent at night to Abu Taybah, who cupped him, and he gave him his wage."
"11930","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit."
"11931","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Umar ibn al-Khattab entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was on a mat that had left marks on his side, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you took bedding softer than this; he said: What have I to do with the world? By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, my example and the example of the world is only like a rider traveling on a hot summer day, who shades under a tree for an hour of the day, then moves on and leaves it."
"11932","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned toward Uhud and said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it would not please me that Uhud turn into gold for the family of Muhammad, which I spend in the cause of Allah, and that I die on the day I die leaving two dinars of it, except two dinars I prepare for a debt if there is one upon me."
"11933","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: used to spend successive nights folded in hunger, and his family found no supper; he said: And most of their bread was barley bread."
"11934","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died leaving neither dinar nor dirham, nor male nor female slave, and he left his armor mortgaged with a Jew for thirty sa of barley."
"11935","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Nuaym al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You are one-third of the people of Paradise, or: one-half of the people of Paradise."
"11936","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When When the victory of Allah has come and the conquest came down until he completed the surah, he said: The soul of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was announced to him when it came down; he said: So he exerted himself more strenuously than ever before in the matter of the Hereafter, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said after that: The conquest and the victory of Allah have come, and the people of Yemen have come; so a man said: O Messenger of Allah, and what are the people of Yemen? He said: A people with delicate hearts, soft hearts; faith is Yemeni, and understanding is Yemeni."
"11937","Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it, and he added: And wisdom is Yemeni."
"11938","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fought a battle, and did not finish with them until evening kept him from the Asr prayer past the time he used to guard; so when he finished with them, he looked and found the Asr prayer had been overtaken by evening, so he prayed; and when he finished his prayer, he supplicated against his enemy and said: O Allah, whoever diverted us from the middle prayer, fill their houses with fire, fill their bellies with fire, and fill their graves with fire."
"11939","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in one of his expeditions, and a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the heedless ones? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept silent and did not answer him a word until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished his expedition and circumambulated, and there was a boy who had fallen from a litter, and there he was; so his caller called: Where is the one who asked about the heedless ones? So the man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he forbade killing their children and said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"11940","Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When When the victory of Allah has come and the conquest came down, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called Fatimah and said: My soul has been announced to me; so she wept; so he said to her: Do not weep, for you are the first of my family to join me; so she laughed; then one of the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw her and said to her: I saw you weep and laugh; she said: He said to me: My soul has been announced to me, so I wept; then he said: Do not weep, for you are the first of my family to join me, so I laughed."
"11941","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Ubayd ibn Khalaf al-Qatii narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his uncle al-Abbas: O uncle, supplicate often for well-being."
"11942","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Dubaa bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I intend Hajj, should I stipulate? He said: Yes; I said: What should I say? He said: Say: Labbayk, O Allah, Labbayk, my place of release is wherever You detain me."
"11943","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yahya Sahib al-Basri narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn al-Kumayt narrated to us, and Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, both saying: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: performed qunut for a month in all the prayers: Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib and Isha."
"11944","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili and al-Husayn ibn al-Kumayt narrated to us, both saying: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Aslam, may Allah grant them safety, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive them."
"11945","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stayed in Makkah seventeen nights shortening the prayer."
"11946","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub and Asim al-Ahwal, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: passed by a pot, so he took a bone from it and ate from it, then prayed and did not perform ablution."
"11947","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah, Exalted is He, chose Ibrahim for intimate friendship, and chose Musa for speech, and chose Muhammad for the Vision."
"11948","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Musa ibn Muhammad al-Ansari narrated to us, from Asim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had cupping done while in ihram, and said: Ihram is more severe than fasting."
"11949","Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a man placing his foot on the cheek of a sheep while sharpening his blade, and it was looking at him with its eyes; he said: Why not before this? Do you want to kill it twice?"
"11950","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ibn Uthman ibn Kathir ibn Dinar al-Himsi narrated to us, I think him Yahya, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Hamrah, from Mansur, from Asim al-Bajali, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever does not press his nose to the ground along with his forehead when prostrating, his prayer is not valid."
"11951","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, Abd Allah al-Danaj narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to me, he said: I prayed with Abu Hurayrah, and he used to say takbir when rising and when lowering; so I mentioned that to Ibn Abbas, and he said: May you lose your mother, is that not the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him?"
"11952","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: married Maymunah while they were both in ihram."
"11953","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad al-Kufi, Humayd and Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: slept until snoring was heard from him, then prayed and did not repeat ablution."
"11954","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata al-Attar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about one who approaches his wife while she is menstruating, he said: He should give a dinar in charity, and if he does not find, then half a dinar."
"11955","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Makhlad al-Wasiti narrated to us, from his father, from Sallam Abu al-Mundhir, from Matar al-Warraq, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: married Maymunah while he was out of ihram."
"11956","Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mughirah ibn Muslim, from Matar al-Warraq, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever claims a dream he did not see will be commanded to tie two grains of barley together, and whoever makes an image will be commanded to breathe into it, and whoever eavesdrops on the talk of a people fleeing from him, molten lead will be placed in his ear."
"11957","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, and Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Balkhi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rafi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Qudamah al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: did not prostrate in any of the Mufassal since he moved to Madinah."
"11958","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A Bedouin man died and had no agnate heirs, but he had a freed slave whom he had freed, so that was raised to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Did he not anger for his anger and approve for his approval? They said: Yes; and he gave him the property of his freedman as inheritance."
"11959","Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn Ayyub al-Madini al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed whoever brands on the face."
"11960","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abd al-Karim informed me that he heard Ikrimah mentioning from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of the Conquest: Allah, Majestic is His remembrance, made Makkah sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth, so it is sacred by the sacredness of Allah until the Day of Resurrection; its game is not to be startled, its trees are not to be cut, its herbage is not to be uprooted, and its lost property is not lawful except for one who announces it; so al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said: Except idhkhir, O Messenger of Allah, for it is needed for the blacksmith and the houses; so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was silent for a while, then said: Except idhkhir, for it is lawful."
"11961","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, and Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us, all saying: Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat al-Kindi narrated to us, from Ilba ibn Ahmad al-Yashkuri, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drew four lines on the ground, then said: Do you know what this is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best women of the people of Paradise are Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Fatimah bint Muhammad, Maryam bint Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh."
"11962","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hurayth narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Ilba ibn Ahmad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and the sacrifice came, so we shared seven in a cow and ten in a camel."
"11963","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abi Hariz, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt or maternal aunt."
"11964","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah, from Abi Hariz, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade marrying a woman together with the paternal aunt and the maternal aunt, and said: If you do that, you will sever your kinship ties."
"11965","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Said Abu Ghaylan al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: I heard Affan ibn Jubayr al-Tai, from Abi Hariz al-Azdi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A day under a just imam is better than sixty years of worship, and a prescribed punishment carried out on earth in its right is more purifying in it than forty years of rain."
"11966","Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Umar ibn Farrukh, seller of saddle packs, narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Zubayr, from Ikrimah, he said: I saw in the Sacred Mosque an old man praying, when he raised his head he said takbir, and when he lowered his head, and when he rose between the two takbirs he said takbir, so I disapproved of that, so I went to Ibn Abbas and informed him, and he said: May you lose your mother, that is the prayer of Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"11967","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Said ibn al-Musayyab ibn Sharik narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Umar ibn Farrukh, seller of saddle packs, narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Zubayr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: had cupping done and gave the cupper a dinar."
"11968","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Umar ibn Farrukh, keeper of saddle packs, narrated to us, Habib ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling fruit until it becomes edible, and wool on the back, and milk in the udder."
"11969","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Yala ibn Hakim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Maiz ibn Malik came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said to him: Perhaps you kissed, or touched, or caressed; he said: No; he said: Did you do such and such? Without euphemism; he said: Yes; so he ordered him stoned."
"11970","Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hakkam narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Yala ibn Hakim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying, a sheep came running in front of him, so he raced it until he pressed his belly to the wall."
"11971","Al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Missisi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Mansur al-Qadi narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yala ibn Hakim narrating from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out during his illness with his head bound with a cloth, sat on the minbar, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: There is none among the people more generous to me with himself and his wealth than Abu Bakr ibn Abi Quhafah, and had I taken any of the people as an intimate friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr, but the brotherhood of Islam is better; then he said: No small door in the mosque shall remain except it is closed, except the small door of Abu Bakr."
"11972","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muslim ibn Sallam narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas used to wear khazz silk, and it was remarked to him, so he said: Only pure silk was forbidden."
"11973","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Mubarak Abu Amr narrated to us, Ikrimah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, in a raised report, he said: Whoever dies with date-wine vapor in his belly, Allah will expose him before the witnesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"11974","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, in a raised report, he said: There is none except his saying is taken and left, other than the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"11975","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya narrated to us, Saiqah narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Harun ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The food of two rivals showing off was forbidden."
"11976","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, Harun ibn Musa al-Nahwi narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Avoid rhymed prose in supplication, for I knew the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his Companions did not do that."
"11977","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"11978","Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi and Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Maiz ibn Malik came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: He committed adultery, so he turned away from him, then asked his people: Is he mad? They said: There is no harm in him; he said: Did you do it with her? He said: Yes; so he ordered him stoned, and he was taken away and he did not pray over him."
"11979","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Snakes are the transformed jinn, just as monkeys and pigs were transformed from the Children of Israel."
"11980","Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Makhlad al-Laythi narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Safiyyah: Stipulate that my place of release is wherever You detain me."
"11981","Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad narrated to us, Amr ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever imagines in his prayer that he has broken ablution should not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."
"11982","Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad narrated to us, Amr ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Bishr narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my sister vowed to perform Hajj walking; he said: Let her ride, for Allah, Exalted is He, is in no need of her walking."
"11983","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Nuaym al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying, then Abu Jahl came and forbade him to pray, so Allah the Exalted sent down: Then let him call his associates, We will call the wardens of Hell; Ibn Abbas said: Had he done so, the wardens would have seized him."
"11984","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah informed us, and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, all of them from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visited a Bedouin while ill; he said: And when he visited a sick person he used to say: No harm, a purification, if Allah wills; so he said: You say purification? No, rather it is a fever boiling over an old man, consigning him to the graves; so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Then yes, so be it; and the wording is from the hadith of Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar."
"11985","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi al-Tarsusi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Farra narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of Badr: This is Jibril, peace be upon him, holding the forelock of a horse, with the gear of war upon him."
"11986","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he came from Makkah, young boys of the Banu Abd al-Muttalib met him, so he carried one in front of him and another behind him."
"11987","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had cupping done and gave the cupper his wage, and had he known it impure he would not have given him."
"11988","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, circumambulated on a camel, and whenever he came to the Corner he gestured toward it."
"11989","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Seven were made unlawful by lineage, and seven by marriage ties, and he recited this verse in Surah al-Nisa."
"11990","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah made Makkah sacred, so it was not lawful for anyone before me, nor is it lawful for anyone after me, and it was only made lawful for me for an hour of the day; its herbage is not to be uprooted, its trees are not to be cut, its game is not to be startled, and its lost property is not to be picked up except by one who announces it; al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, except idhkhir for our craftsmen; he said: Except idhkhir."
"11991","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hamid ibn Adam al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Islam is ten shares, and he has failed who has no share in it: the testimony that there is no god but Allah, and it is the creed; the second, prayer, and it is the natural disposition; the third, zakat, and it is purification; the fourth, fasting, and it is the shield; the fifth, Hajj, and it is the law; the sixth, jihad, and it is warfare; the seventh, commanding the right, and it is fidelity; the eighth, forbidding the wrong, and it is the proof; the ninth, the community, and it is fellowship; and the tenth, obedience, and it is protection."
"11992","Uthman ibn Khalid ibn Amr al-Sulafi al-Himsi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Himsi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Humayd, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: We have no evil likeness; the one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit."
"11993","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever listens to the talk of a people who dislike it, molten lead will be poured into his ears; and whoever claims a dream will be charged with tying a grain of barley, and he will be punished, and he will not tie it; and whoever makes an image will be punished until he breathes the soul into it, and he will not breathe."
"11994","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, embraced me and said: O Allah, teach him wisdom."
"11995","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Khalid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the husband of Barirah was a slave called Mughith, as if I am looking at him circling behind her weeping with his tears flowing upon his beard; so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to al-Abbas: O Abbas, do you not marvel at the intensity of Mughith's love for Barirah, and the intensity of Barirah's hatred for Mughith; so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: If only you took him back, for he is the father of your child; she said: O Messenger of Allah, do you command me? He said: I am only an intercessor; she said: Then I have no need of him."
"11996","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Khalid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to the watering place and asked for drink; so al-Abbas said to al-Fadl: Go to your mother and bring the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a drink from her; so he said: Give me to drink; he said: O Messenger of Allah, they put their hands in it; so he said: Give me to drink; so he drank from it, then came to Zamzam while they were giving drink and working in it, so he said: Work, for you are upon righteous work; then he said: Were it not that you would be overcome, I would descend until I place upon this, meaning his shoulder, and he pointed to his shoulder."
"11997","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Where the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited aloud, we recited aloud, and where he kept silent, we kept silent."
"11998","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out in Ramadan to Hunayn, with the people differing, some fasting and some breaking fast; so when he settled upon his mount, he called for a vessel of milk or water and drank it; he said: So he placed it upon his mount, then the people looked, so those breaking fast said to those fasting: Break fast."
"11999","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Musa narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that when Ali ibn Abi Talib wanted to consummate marriage with Fatimah, they said: Bring something; he said: I find nothing; so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Where is your Hutami armor?"
"12000","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was not asked about anything on the day of sacrifice except he said: No harm, no harm."
